inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_4 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:33 lap 1 grain: still paused on PIPELINES-GREEN; today's state of that dep: spiral, dice, polyglot, alphabet, x, eoie all red on the 06:48 push for causes fixed in working trees (rustix Linux cfg, dir-tree-html UTF-8, mix deps.get, x protocol.spi, eoie partial src commit); i574n.github has no Actions runs at all (gh run list 404) Next: resume when PIPELINES-GREEN shows the next push runs green; check whether i574n.github needs a workflow at all")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_5 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:25Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:25 lap 2 grain, corrects lap 1 (i574n.github has no Actions runs at all): the local C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github checkout is the i574n/.github repo (git remote origin), not i574n/i574n.github (which does not exist, hence the 404). i574n/.github has a workflow (gh-pages.yml + actions.lock) and runs: the 10-18 17:49Z push run was green (1h40m) and deployed; the 22:13Z push run failed after 1h18m but its Ubuntu-leg publish still deployed at 23:32Z (Pages built at i574n.github.io/.github/). So it does need its workflow (it is the backlog and workflow.livemd host) and is one more repo PIPELINES-GREEN must see green. Still paused on PIPELINES-GREEN; the list of repos to watch is spiral, dice, polyglot, alphabet, x, eoie, blog, dir-tree-html, tibia and i574n/.github. Next: when PIPELINES-GREEN reports the next push wave, read each repo's newest push run conclusion with gh run list -R i574n/<repo> -L 1")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_6 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 6u32, "2026-10-19T14:01Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:01 lap 3 grain: the reference chain made explicit. i574n.github/scripts/workflow.ps1 runs init.ps1 (clones spiral, dir-tree-html, polyglot, dice, alphabet, tibia beside it) then workflow.livemd = build.ps1, outdated.ps1, publish.ps1, and build.ps1 builds spiral, dir-tree-html, polyglot (Stop on failure), then dice, alphabet, tibia with -OnError Continue. Its CI twin is i574n/.github's gh-pages workflow, so that run is the end-to-end oracle. Its last red run (39171310951, 10-18 22:13Z, Ubuntu leg) shows the open breakages in order: a polyglot step referencing an undefined PackageManager variable (Continue), Cells mix step exit 1 under spiral/apps/cells (Continue), spiral/apps/wasm run printing usage (-e, --exception), alphabet exits 100 and 70, near wallet test:e2e timing out on config.webServer after 60 s, and the publish whose half dist turned the page 404 (TREE-PAGES note 11). So the order of fixes for this item is the PIPELINES-GREEN list plus near-wallet e2e and alphabet's 100/70. Still paused on PIPELINES-GREEN. Next: after the next .github run, diff its failed steps against this list")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_7 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:31Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:31 lap 4 grain: read the alphabet part of the reference run's last red log (39171310951). The exit 100s are by design: alphabet/scripts/init.ps1:32-35 runs apt-get update and apt install pandoc fonts-nanum-coding once with sudo and once without (container fallback), all -OnError Continue, so the no-sudo pair always fails on a runner (Permission denied) and the Windows leg's WSL apt cannot find fonts-nanum-coding; harmless noise. The real alphabet failure is exit 70 from cargo binstall -y tectonic (init.ps1:38): binstall falls back to cargo install tectonic 0.17.0, which fails (exit 101) without the TeX/harfbuzz system libraries, while alphabet's own workflow avoids that with wtfjoke/setup-tectonic@v3.1.5 before its build. The reference workflow lacked that step, so alphabet's PDF documents could never build there. Fixed in the tree: i574n/.github gh-pages.yml gains the same setup-tectonic step before pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1, and gh actions-lock pinned it in .github/workflows/actions.lock (8a63d07, additions only), per the lockfile rule. Needs the user's push. Next: on the next .github run, check that alphabet's documents build passes and that the cargo binstall tectonic line reports the preinstalled binary")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_8 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 8u32, "2026-10-19T15:18Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:18 lap 5 grain: found and fixed the near wallet e2e failure of the reference run (39171310951, Ubuntu leg): playwright runs webServer.command through sh, and the command was pwsh -c with a double-quoted script holding dollar-job, so sh expanded dollar-job to nothing and pwsh got = Start-Job ... (log: [WebServer] The term = is not recognized), the server never came up and playwright timed out after 60 s on config.webServer. On Windows cmd leaves the dollar alone, which is why it only failed on Linux. Fix in the spiral tree: lib/spiral/near/wallet/serve.ps1 (new, same steps: cd dist, Start-Job bunx --bun ssl-serve --ssl, 60 s, stop, receive) and playwright.config.ts runs pwsh -NoProfile -File serve.ps1, so no shell sees a dollar sign. Parse-checked, LF; not run (playwright e2e needs the built dist; it runs in spiral's and .github's CI after the user's push). Also checked: the PackageManager line of lap 3 no longer exists in any script under C:\\home\\git (no match), so that step is gone from the list. Remaining from the reference run: Cells mix exit 1, spiral/apps/wasm usage print, alphabet tectonic (fixed lap 4, unpushed), half-dist publish (fixed, unpushed).")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_9 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 9u32, "2026-10-19T15:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:36 lap 6 grain, the Cells mix step of the reference run has two causes, one per leg. Ubuntu: mix spiral.html ran in spiral/apps/cells before any mix deps.get (Unchecked dependencies: kino not available). The working tree's scripts/core.ps1 already has the fix (Invoke-PwshNotebook runs local.hex, local.rebar and deps.get when deps/kino is missing; uncommitted, 8 lines). Windows: Cannot remove symlink .../polyglot/deps/spiral/apps/cells/_build/dev/lib/spiral_cells/priv: not owner. The same Cells tree was reached through polyglot/deps/spiral (a symlink to spiral) and through spiral itself, so mix kept relinking priv under two paths. Fixed in the tree: core.ps1 now computes cellsDir with ResolveLink, so mix always runs from the real spiral/apps/cells path (checked: polyglot/deps/spiral/scripts/../apps/cells resolves to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\apps\\cells, and the direct route is unchanged). Edit to spiral scripts/core.ps1 noted for the other lanes. Still open: spiral/apps/wasm build.ps1 run prints clap usage (Usage: spiral_wasm.exe --wasm <wasm>) because it runs with no --wasm argument; next lap.")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_10 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 10u32, "2026-10-19T15:49Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:49 lap 7: the last item of the reference-run list is already resolved in HEAD. The spiral/apps/wasm usage print came from running spiral_wasm with no arguments. Since 668568ac (10-19 02:48) apps/wasm/build.ps1 runs it with --help as a deliberate run check: exit 0 and the --wasm argument expected, otherwise RUST-FAILED. So the Usage lines are now the passing check, not an error. Every breakage of run 39171310951 now has a fix in a tree: polyglot PackageManager (gone), Cells mix (deps.get guard + ResolveLink, unpushed), apps/wasm (HEAD), alphabet tectonic (unpushed), near wallet e2e (serve.ps1, unpushed), half-dist publish (unpushed). The next .github run after the user's push is the test; the item stays Paused on PIPELINES-GREEN until then.")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_11 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 11u32, "2026-10-19T16:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:32 lap 8 grain: post-switch check of the reference run path: i574n.github workflow.livemd runs build.ps1 -> spiral/scripts/build.ps1 -> apps/spiral/build.ps1 (whose first step already exports spiral.livemd to spiral.spi through apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 --export-only), then apps/wasm, apps/plot, lib/spiral. The core switch moved apps/spiral's source of truth edits into the livemd, which this path already exports, so it adds no step or prerequisite. Still Paused on the push")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_12 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 12u32, "2026-10-19T16:57Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:57 lap 9 grain: trigger check for the reference run: i574n.github/.github/workflows/gh-pages.yml has only a push trigger (no schedule and no workflow_dispatch), so 39171310951 (10-18 22:13Z) stays the latest reference run and nothing reruns it until the user pushes i574n.github; a push of spiral alone retriggers spiral's own run (it also has a daily 13:15Z schedule) but not this one. Since the reference run builds siblings from their remote mains, the order is: push spiral, dice, alphabet, polyglot first, then i574n.github")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_13 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 13u32, "2026-10-19T17:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:32 lap 10 grain: rechecked i574n/.github (the i574n.github checkout's remote): latest gh-pages run is still 39171310951 (failure, 10-18 22:13Z); the only later run is a pages-build-deployment success (39176952821, 23:32Z), which is the Pages publish of the existing gh-pages branch, not a workflow rerun; main is still 9dd1144e. Unchanged: only a push of i574n.github retests the workflow. Next: user's push (after the sibling pushes)")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_14 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 14u32, "2026-10-19T17:51Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:51 lap 11 grain: what the retest push needs, measured (git rev-list/status, read only): no repo has unpushed commits (spiral, eoie, dice, alphabet, polyglot, i574n.github all 0 ahead of their i574n remote main), so everything waiting is uncommitted work in the trees: spiral 251 paths, eoie 55, dice 12, polyglot 6, alphabet 5, i574n.github 4 (backlog state). The order stays siblings first (spiral, eoie, dice, alphabet, polyglot), then i574n.github, whose push alone triggers its gh-pages workflow. Next: user's commits + pushes")
inl spiral_independent () = Task ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", "Make spiral independent of polyglot, then split what remains of polyglot into descriptive repos; 2026-10-08: lib/spiral/*.fsx gone (FSX-FREE, spiral_runtime.fs instead), 4 compiler samples resolve their lib through spiral itself instead of deps/polyglot/deps/spiral (20 rows parity, residuals unchanged), apps/wasm builds natively on Windows; remaining polyglot mentions: env.ps1 and Kino core-package fallbacks (../polyglot), Kino polyglot_root option alias, docs; 23:2x dir-tree-html left spiral for its own repo; consumers reach it through spiral scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, not polyglot paths; 2026-10-12 inventory (code files only): what still ties spiral to polyglot is shallow, three steps: (1) naming: `namespace Polyglot` in spiral_compiler.fs, host Program.fs, runtime-compat PolyglotCommon.fs, RootNamespace in SpiralCompilerCore/SpiralCompiler fsproj and gear-dev.ps1, and two stack-trace filters matching \"Polyglot\" (spiral_compiler.fs ~133373, ~188068) -> rename to Spiral in one ladder; (2) consumers: dice and alphabet reach spiral as deps/polyglot/deps/spiral (init.ps1, package.spiproj packageDir, CI checkout) -> clone spiral directly as deps/spiral (mirror dice -> alphabet); (3) then drop the polyglot fallbacks: env.ps1:129-130 (VS Code Plugin core path), kino domain_compiler.ex:49, toolchain.ex:21, notebook.ex @lib_rels polyglot entries, kino.ex polyglot_root/SPIRAL_KINO_POLYGLOT_ROOT option; leave mentions in docs/history and the contract_*_polyglot_* sample names alone; step (2) is a multi-repo decision for the user: dice (and alphabet) use polyglot for far more than reaching spiral: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 in every build script, polyglot/lib/fsharp (Common.fs, Notebooks.livemd, open Polyglot), polyglot's parser app and init toolchains, polyglot/deps/hyperui css; cloning spiral directly in dice would leave two spiral copies (deps/spiral and polyglot/deps/spiral) unless polyglot stops vendoring spiral or the shared helpers move (core.ps1 into spiral or its own repo); step (1) and (3) can proceed independently; user decision 2026-10-12 19:05: once spiral no longer needs polyglot, split what remains into focused repos named for what they are and archive polyglot; 2026-10-13 22:59 the spiral-split gear splitter (scripts/gear-dev.ps1, bench-split.ps1, build-splitter.ps1, tmp/splitter, lanes/splitter) was removed at the user's request: idle since early October (234 runs Sep 26-Oct 1, then 21), built for gpt5parallel's 159k lines; use build.ps1 -Configuration Debug -CoreSource <copy> for candidates", Epic, P2, D6, 60u32, Active, "", "repos,polyglot", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_independent () = Planning ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_spiral_independent_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:56Z", "lane-b", "next step mapped (step 3, Kino): 5 fallback sites: kino.ex:137-141 polyglot_root opt/app env/SPIRAL_KINO_POLYGLOT_ROOT, notebook.ex:24-34 deps/polyglot/deps/spiral lib paths, toolchain.ex:21 ../polyglot core package, domain_compiler.ex:62 ../../../polyglot/deps; dice/alphabet still reach spiral via deps/polyglot/deps/spiral, so the notebook.ex lib paths go only after step 2")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 2u32, "2026-10-15T04:00Z", "lane-b", "00:00 lane B: step 3 Kino part LANDED (uncommitted): polyglot_root option/app env/SPIRAL_KINO_POLYGLOT_ROOT alias removed (kino.ex, notebook.ex option list, kino_test, notebook_test, README), toolchain.ex default_package_dir is spiral's own deps clone only (the ../polyglot candidate never matched in any CI layout: in dice the spiral root is deps/polyglot/deps/spiral), spi/domain_compiler.ex the same; no consumer in spiral/dice/alphabet/polyglot/eoie used the alias (git grep); left: notebook.ex @lib_rels deps/polyglot/deps/spiral entries (dice still reaches spiral that way, step 2), env.ps1:129-130")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: Kino's polyglot fallbacks and the polyglot_root alias are removed (lane B, uncommitted). Next grain: list remaining polyglot references in spiral (scripts and docs).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 4u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: step 1 staged and reviewed: pack-a/namespace-spiral.ps1 renames namespace Polyglot to Spiral in core, host, 3 refs, both fsproj RootNamespace, compat PolyglotCommon.fs, profile scripts and formatter fsx (15 files). The 3 Polyglot stack-frame filters on gpt5parallel-only sides stay (pair-drift rejects one-sided edits; they filter nothing after the rename). Pack: night pack 10-17 (scripts %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\packs\\night-1017, each with -DryRun; final review single-flight-20261017-053315 on the exact pack: 6,906 rows, DISAGREE 0, residual-only Zig 457 and Rust 415, 3 intended Rust exit cells (shown as 2 NATIVE-DIFF rows); builds in single-flight, hopacsota and gpt5parallel; hopacsota inline and random:23 equal single-flight on every compile and residual cell; corpus 144 of 144; Zig at C speed on the bench).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:33 lap 1 grain: step 1 shipped: the compiler file declares namespace Spiral (0 namespace Polyglot left), from the 10-17 night pack-a rename; remaining polyglot coupling to measure: who still resolves through deps/polyglot (dice and alphabet build.ps1 dot-source ../deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib) Next: grep every repo's scripts for deps/polyglot paths and list which could point at spiral directly")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 6u32, "2026-10-19T12:50Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:50 lap 2 grain: deps/polyglot references in tracked scripts/yml/spiproj: dice 25 in 14 files, alphabet 12 in 8, spiral 1 (env.ps1:135, a package-dir fallback to polyglot's The-Spiral-Language clone), x/blog/dir-tree-html/eoie/i574n.github 0; dice's reduce to two patterns: polyglot's own scripts/core.ps1 (11x) and spiral reached through polyglot/deps/spiral (lib.ps1 5x, dir-tree-html.ps1, publish-tree.ps1) Next: diff the function sets of polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and spiral/scripts/core.ps1; if spiral's covers dice's calls, dice and alphabet can clone spiral directly")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 7u32, "2026-10-19T12:50Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:50 follow-up: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 defines no functions; it is a forwarder that finds spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (deps/spiral or a sibling clone, else clones it) and dot-sources it. So every dice and alphabet dependency on polyglot is really on spiral: the switch is dice/alphabet init cloning spiral into deps/spiral and rewriting 25 + 12 paths (deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 -> deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1, deps/polyglot/deps/spiral -> deps/spiral), mirrored in both repos (alphabet mirrors dice)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 8u32, "2026-10-19T13:26Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:26 lap 2 grain: prepared lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/rewrite-deps.ps1 (dry run by default, -Apply writes) for dice and alphabet together (alphabet mirrors dice). Rules: deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/ -> deps/spiral/ and deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 -> deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1 over tracked .ps1/.spiproj/.yml/.toml/.json, plus EnsureSymbolicLink ../deps/spiral -> ../../spiral in scripts/init.ps1 where missing (dice lacks it; alphabet has it since earlier), inserted after polyglot's init call so the sibling spiral clone exists. Equivalence checked: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is a 13-line forwarder that dot-sources spiral's scripts/core.ps1 (or clones spiral beside polyglot), polyglot/deps/spiral is a link to the sibling C:\\home\\git\\spiral, and every rewritten target exists in spiral (scripts/core.ps1, lib/spiral/lib.ps1, apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1, scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, scripts/publish-tree.ps1, apps/spiral/build.ps1). Dry run: 22 files change (dice 14, alphabet 8). 4 deps/polyglot references stay on purpose because they name polyglot-owned files: dice lib/fsharp/build.ps1:24 (polyglot lib/fsharp/Common.fs), both init.ps1 polyglot links, alphabet init.ps1:28 (polyglot apps/parser build). Not applied: it changes CI wiring in two repos, so it goes with a user push; decision recorded: apply in one step for both repos, then run both repos' build.ps1 (heavy) before the push. Next: decide whether Common.fs and apps/parser can move to spiral (the last two polyglot needs of dice/alphabet)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 9u32, "2026-10-19T14:04Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:04 lap 3 grain: decided the two polyglot-owned leftovers. (1) polyglot/apps/parser (F# JsonParser/Parser exported from .livemd) is built by both inits (dice scripts/init.ps1, alphabet scripts/init.ps1:28) but nothing in dice or alphabet reads its output (grep for JsonParser, Parser.fs, apps/parser/Parser: 0 files in either repo), so the build step is dead work: rewrite-deps.ps1 now drops it from both inits. (2) polyglot/lib/fsharp/Common.fs (50 lines) stays for now: its only dice consumer is lib/fsharp/build.ps1 (the F# runtime modules of the dice lib), which retires with the F# lane (bold native goals), so moving it into spiral would only move dead weight. Also added rule ../../polyglot/deps/spiral/ -> ../../spiral/ (dice init still built spiral apps and dir-tree-html through polyglot's link to the sibling spiral). Dry run: 22 files; dice init now links deps/spiral, drops the parser build, and builds apps/spiral, apps/wasm and dir-tree-html from ../../spiral directly. Left deps/polyglot references: Common.fs and the two polyglot links (needed only for Common.fs and polyglot's own init). Next: after the F# lib of dice is retired or moved, drop polyglot from dice/alphabet entirely; apply rewrite-deps.ps1 -Apply with a user push")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 10u32, "2026-10-19T15:19Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:19 lap 5 grain on step (1) naming: the namespace rename is done (spiral_compiler.fs has namespace Spiral, no namespace Polyglot left), but the two stack-trace filters the 10-12 inventory listed still keep only frames containing Polyglot (spiral_compiler.fs:127534 debugTraceAt, :185367 the FatalError path for NullReference/InvalidOperation/... exceptions). Since the rename they match nothing, so an internal compiler exception reports only its message and the debug term trace has no frames: a silent regression from the rename. Staged lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/stack-frames.py (both filters -> Spiral.; dry run 2 anchors match) to ride pack 7; matrix.psd1 has no pin naming those exception types, so no pin changes expected. Step (3) leftovers in Cells: notebook.ex @lib_rels lines 30 and 33 (deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral, polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral) stay until dice/alphabet drop polyglot (rewrite-deps.ps1); fsi_session.ex:7 is a doc mention only.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 11u32, "2026-10-19T15:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:36 lap 6 grain, step (3) inventory and the first cut. Polyglot mentions left in spiral code: Cells notebook.ex @lib_rels (2, waiting on rewrite-deps), fsi_session.ex (doc only), lib file_system.spi:761 (a test that also accepts a source dir named polyglot, harmless until vendoring ends), and apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/env.ps1:135-136, Get-SpiralPackageDir's two polyglot fallbacks. The env.ps1 pair is dead: the first candidate, spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language, exists locally and is cloned by scripts/init-app-build.ps1 in CI. Staged lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py (dry run: the anchor matches once), queued for main after the switch accept, because the switch may rewrite how core- resolves. Also today: spiral scripts/core.ps1 now resolves the Cells dir through ResolveLink, so the polyglot/deps/spiral route no longer runs mix from a second path (WORKFLOW-END-TO-END note).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 12u32, "2026-10-19T15:56Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:56 lap 7 grain: rewrite-deps.ps1 rechecked against today's trees (dry run, still 22 files) and taught to keep its own TODO block true. After the rewrite, dice/scripts/init.ps1's SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT block (which says dice still reaches spiral through polyglot) would be false, so the script now replaces it with: dice keeps deps/polyglot only for lib/fsharp/build.ps1's Common.fs (polyglot/lib/fsharp); drop this link and the polyglot init once the F# lib of dice retires or Common.fs moves (each line at most 120 columns). The dry-run diff shows the swap; the harvest will then point at the remaining tie only.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 13u32, "2026-10-19T16:33Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:33 lap 8 grain: post-switch census of spiral's remaining code ties to polyglot (apps/cells/lib + compiler scripts, case-insensitive): env.ps1:135-136 (the two VS Code Plugin core fallbacks; drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py dry run still matches its anchor after the switch) and cells notebook.ex:30 and :33 (lib_rels for deps/polyglot/deps/spiral, the route dice and alphabet use until rewrite-deps lands). The older step-3 ties (domain_compiler.ex, toolchain.ex, kino polyglot_root option) no longer exist; fsi_session.ex:7 is a history mention. So step 3 is 2 staged lines now plus 2 lib_rels lines that wait on step 2")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 14u32, "2026-10-19T16:39Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 12:39 stack-frames.py taken out of pack 7: both of its filters live on gpt5parallel-only sides (PartEval at 127534, SignalRSupervisor at 185367), so the Release build's pair-drift check stopped the build (changed only on the gpt5parallel side), exactly as the 10-17 note predicted; reverted in the tree (pair-drift clean). The dead Polyglot filters can only go with gpt5parallel's retirement (HOPACSOTA-P6) or with a mirrored single-flight change.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 15u32, "2026-10-19T17:00Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:00 lap 9 grain: dry run of rewrite-deps.ps1 rechecked against what it leaves behind: (1) alphabet's EnsureSymbolicLink deps/polyglot (init.ps1:25) becomes dead after the rewrite, because alphabet has no lib/fsharp (so no Common.fs), its parser build line is dropped and every deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is mapped to deps/spiral; the link should go in the same rewrite, unlike dice's, which Common.fs still needs. (2) The rewrite covers only deps/polyglot paths; sibling-path uses of polyglot stay: alphabet scripts/build.ps1:8, init.ps1:20 and :23, apps/hangul/build.ps1:8, and dice scripts/init.ps1:20 and :26 (core.ps1 dot-source and the polyglot init). These are the last ties to plan for, with the same core.ps1 mapping to ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 16u32, "2026-10-19T17:34Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:34 lap 10 grain: rewrite-deps.ps1 extended for lap 9's gap, dry run 24 files (was 22), parse 0 errors. Found first why a plain path map was unsafe: dice init.ps1 sources ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 BEFORE polyglot's init clones spiral, and that core.ps1 is only a shim that clones spiral itself when missing; so mapping it to ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1 alone breaks a fresh runner. The script now (1) adds a spiral clone (Set-Location .., git clone spiral.git, git pull) to the single polyglot clone block of each init.ps1, keeping its indentation, (2) maps ../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 to ../spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (dice init, alphabet init, alphabet scripts/build.ps1, apps/hangul/build.ps1, which already sources ../../../spiral/lib), (3) drops alphabet's dead deps/polyglot link. After it, alphabet has 0 deps/polyglot references; dice keeps only Common.fs + its link. Caveat: alphabet -fast on a never-initialized tree no longer self-clones spiral (fast assumes an initialized tree). Next: user/main go for --Apply in dice + alphabet together (alphabet mirrors dice), then their workflow.ps1 runs")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 17u32, "2026-10-19T17:52Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:52 lap 11 grain: rewrite-deps.ps1 now parse-checks every rewritten .ps1 in memory (PowerShell Parser.ParseInput) and refuses the whole run if one would not parse, so --Apply cannot write a broken init.ps1; dry run: all 24 rewritten files parse (files changed: 24, no parse refusal). Next: go for -Apply in dice + alphabet together, then their workflow.ps1 runs")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_18 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 18u32, "2026-10-19T17:52Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:52 follow-up: made the refusal claim true for -Apply too: writes are collected and done only after every file was rewritten and parsed (before, files earlier in the loop were written before a later refusal); dry run unchanged (24 files), dice tree untouched (12 dirty paths before and after)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_19 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 19u32, "2026-10-19T18:19Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 14:19 lap 12: dice keeps deps/polyglot only for lib/fsharp Common.fs, and dice_fsharp.fs uses it in exactly one place (line 95, trace Debug (...) _locals). Common.trace only maps its own TraceLevel onto SpiralTrace.TraceLevel, so dice_fsharp.livemd can call SpiralTrace.trace SpiralTrace.TraceLevel.Debug directly and drop the Common.fs import and the open Polyglot/Common lines (livemd 37, 41, 45) plus build.ps1:24's module, which removes the last polyglot link")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_20 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 20u32, "2026-10-19T22:48Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 18:48 lap 19 grain: rechecked the three staged applies after main's core-v1 migration of dice, alphabet and polyglot (18:3x, 163 rule edits): dry runs still clean, dice-drop-common.py 5 edits in 3 files (Common.fs import and the one trace call), drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py its 1 env.ps1 anchor, rewrite-deps.ps1 24 files that all parse; the migration touched none of their anchors. Next: main's go for the three applies (dice and alphabet together)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_21 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 21u32, "2026-10-19T23:20Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 19:20 lap 21 grain: stack-frames.py (debugTraceAt and the FatalError path keep only frames containing Polyglot, but the namespace is Spiral now, so both filters drop every frame) did not land with pack 7: its 2 anchors still match today's spiral_compiler.fs. The script now reads newline-preserving (it used read_text, which would normalize line endings) and refuses a file that already filters on Spiral.; checked on a scratch copy (apply, then a second apply refuses). Queue row 67 is still the one to take with the next pack")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_22 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 22u32, "2026-10-19T23:59Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 19:59 main's decision on stack-frames.py: it stays out of every pack until gpt5parallel retires, because both filters it edits sit on the gpt5parallel side of the PartEval section pair, so pair-drift.ps1 stops the build on a one-sided change (that is why pack 7 dropped it). Removed from lab/CALYX-BACKEND/stack-candidate.ps1; queue row 67 is parked on gpt5parallel's retirement")
