inl comment_constants_review () = Task ("COMMENT-CONSTANTS-REVIEW", "Review the 14 unused unit-function constants added in place of sample comments; done 2026-10-11: all 14 located and kept, they are the only rationale a comment-free sample can carry (6 x oracle_must_not_record_current_error; 3 x type_applications_stay_on_one_line_or_the_parser_drops_the_definition; one each of expected_parse_error_at_empty_match, expected_error_lib_extra_is_ambiguous, expected_error_ejp0040, fourth_from_end_one_left_out_its_compile_time_minimization_takes_43_s, excluded_erp_p2p_eight_event_recursive_atomic_payload_outbox_terminal_does_not_compile); every name occurs exactly once in its own file, so all 14 are unused, and none of them reaches a generated file; one name was wrong and is corrected: expected_error_ejp0040 on samples/runaway_inline_match_recursion named the if-nesting limit, which that sample cannot reach because it has no dynamic if branch, only a match recursion over a runtime nat, so hopac reports error[EJP0011] partial evaluation re-entered more than 1024 times (6.5 s probe) and single-flight returns nothing at all within 240 s (killed at 226.7 s, no diagnostic); the marker is now expected_error_ejp0011_reentry_limit and the sample behaves exactly as before", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "samples", "current", "current")
inl lua_wide_integers () = Task ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", "Lua 5.1 doubles: 64-bit integers are inexact (Known rows); exact u64/i64 emulation would lift them", TaskKind, P2, D6, 100u32, Done, "", "backend,lua", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lua_wide_integers () = Planning ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", Minutes 720u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_1 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:35Z", "main-thread", "08:35 scope: 3 Lua Known rows, all from 64-bit: ts_int_wrap (first u64 check), mega_brzozowski runtime_bench and indexed_dfa_state_cardinality (u64 LCG, products up to 2^61). Shared root with GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS (JS numbers). Design for Lua 5.1/WoW: i64/u64 as {hi, lo} 32-bit halves held exactly in doubles. Add/sub with carry via floor division by 2^32; mul via 16-bit limbs so every partial product stays under 2^53; compare hi then lo; and/or/xor per half via WoW's bit library. Emitted only when a program has i64/u64 (as the Gleam prelude does). Next: prototype the u64 mul on the LCG and flip runtime_bench.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_2 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:47Z", "main-thread", "08:47 prototype proven in plain Lua 5.1 (lua51, job tmp/rotation/luawide/lcg.lua): u64 as {hi, lo}; mul by 16-bit limbs (every partial sum < 2^35, exact in doubles), add with carry. 100000 steps of seed*1103515245+12345 mod 2^64 from 42 match BigInteger exactly (hi 4019241552, lo 2060208906), 0.78 s including startup. No bit library is needed for add/mul/compare; only and/or/xor/shift need WoW's bit.* per half. Next: emit these helpers from codegenLua for u64/i64 (i64 = u64 bits plus a sign-aware compare/div/print), then flip ts_int_wrap and runtime_bench.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_3 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: unchanged: prototype only (u64 as {hi,lo} in Lua 5.1). Lua rows 137/137 agree without it because no listed sample needs exact 64-bit math on Lua.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_4 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 4u32, "2026-10-15T11:04Z", "main-thread", "07:04 decision (main, delegated by user 07:0x 'try deciding autonomously for things waiting for my approval'; 'we need all of them sota'): raised P4 -> P2: Lua is a default-backend candidate on compile latency, and a default cannot silently lose 64-bit integer semantics.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_5 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 5u32, "2026-10-15T12:08Z", "lane-b", "08:08 lane-b: codegenLua patch written (patches/lua-wide-integers.ps1, 8 anchors, shared section): i64/u64 stay exact as a Lua number while |v| < 2^53 and as {hi, lo} 32-bit halves beyond, through one spiral_w64 helper table (one local) for add/sub/mul/div/mod/compare/eq/bitwise/shifts/neg/conversions/printf; literals >= 2^53 emit halves. Helper randomized test: 16000 ops x 4 seeds vs Python bigints, 0 mismatches. New sample lua_wide_integers (LCG over u64, i64 min/max, signed div/mod, shifts, bitwise, float/u32 conversions): Debug candidate Lua output = C output line for line; the current compiler prints lcg 1 and wrong values on every line. Lib side (patches/lua-wide-integers-lib.ps1): console write/write_line, format_debug and =./<>. route i64/u64 through spiral_w64. Next: gpt5parallel build, C,Lua list rerun for regressions and timing.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_6 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 6u32, "2026-10-15T13:09Z", "lane-b", "09:09 lane-b proof on a copied harness tree (test.ps1 -Backend C,Lua -Native over the 137-row Lua list plus the 3 Known 64-bit Lua rows plus the new sample; single-flight-20261015-090440 with the 04:05 compiler vs single-flight-20261015-090549 with the Debug candidate): before agree 133, known 3, DISAGREE 1 (lua_wide_integers); after agree 137, known 0, DISAGREE 0. ts_int_wrap, mega_brzozowski runtime_bench and indexed_dfa_state_cardinality now agree with C (Known entries can go). Residuals change on 7 rows; native_closure_union_rec, printf_portable and rust_static_closure_chain still agree. Lua native time summed over the list goes from 56.8 s to 60.0 s; runtime_bench goes from 13.8 s to 17.4 s (20 s row timeout). The gpt5parallel Debug build of the patched core passes (460 s). Patches: lua-wide-integers.ps1 (compiler), lua-wide-integers-lib.ps1, lua-wide-integers-harness.ps1 (adds the sample and the list rows, drops the 3 Known).")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_7 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 7u32, "2026-10-15T18:26Z", "main-thread", "14:26 installed in pack-1k (bless 140535): codegenLua keeps i64/u64 exact via spiral_w64; lua_wide_integers sample agrees with C; ts_int_wrap and indexed_dfa moved from Known to the Lua list. Lib part (base/console/sm'_real through spiral_w64) pending lane B's Kino rerun.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_8 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 8u32, "2026-10-15T20:06Z", "lane-b", "15:0x lane-b: lua-wide-integers-lib + kino-console on a private Kino with the real kz lib (the deps-junction trap fixed): Lua sweep base, console, sm', convert, math, listm', optionm' 96 passed / 8 failed before and after (same Rust/F#-only tests), 765/765 cell outputs byte-identical. No lib cell prints an i64 beyond 2^53, so a Kino Lua-vs-Rust probe (probe/lua_wide.spi) is queued after the Tibia arena.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_9 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 9u32, "2026-10-15T21:42Z", "main-thread", "17:42 lib part blessed in pack-1m (base/console/sm'_real through spiral_w64, Kino console); review changed 1 Lua residual, behaviour 0. Lane B's Kino Lua probe of the printed values runs after the live block.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_10 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 10u32, "2026-10-15T23:10Z", "lane-b", "19:1x lane-b: Kino Lua-vs-Rust probe (probe/lua_wide.spi) inconclusive: the Kino disagreement text shows both Rust and Lua values as f64 (9007199254740992.0 for 9007199254740993i64) and Lua missing the console.write line, while the same program compiled Kino-free prints exact values on Lua 5.1 and 5.4 (9007199254740993, 18446744073709551615, 9007199254740994). Follow-up: Kino-side number normalization/console.write on Lua.")
inl note_of_lua_wide_integers_11 () = Note ("LUA-WIDE-INTEGERS", 11u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: the open Kino-side doubt is resolved: lane B probe lua_wide_print passes on rust and lua with exact values; the record case (format_debug of a record holding a wide i64 printed its halves) is fixed in lib sm_real with a test (format_debug_lua_record_fields).")
inl python_strings_upstream () = Task ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", "CodegenPython string semantics differ from C; upstream section, coordinate with the upstream move", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION", "backend,python,upstream", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_python_strings_upstream () = Planning ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_1 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:33Z", "main-thread", "08:33 scoped: CodegenPython (spiral_compiler.fs ~179183-179196) emits len(s), s[i] and s[a:b]. That is two gaps, not one: code-point vs UTF-8 bytes, and Spiral StringSlice's upto is inclusive (Delphi Copy(from+1, upto-from+1), Zig/Lean upto+1) while Python s[a:b] excludes b. 2026-10-14 run: Python 22 rows, 19 agree; ts_string_slice exits 3 (Known) and ts_int_wrap exits 1 (Known, unbounded ints). Fix shape: helpers over s.encode('utf-8'): len(bytes), bytes[i] as a char, bytes[a:b+1].decode() with the bounds/continuation exit 3. Next: check whether the inclusive-upto bug alone flips ts_string_slice.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_2 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:34Z", "main-thread", "08:34 ts_string_slice is ASCII; its Known reason (code points) is wrong. The cause is the exclusive slice end: emitted v0[1:3] gives 'lp'. Source fixed (CodegenPython StringSlice -> s[a:(b) + 1]); a hand-patched main.py exits 0 like C. Lands with the next pack, which also removes the Known row. UTF-8 byte semantics remain open.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_3 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 3u32, "2026-10-14T15:38Z", "main-thread", "11:38 the corpus check (lane B's lib sweep on the pack-1b candidate) found the matching lib workaround: lib/spiral/sm'.spi slice's Python arm adds 1 to 'to' whenever a value is dynamic (to_py), compensating for the exclusive codegen. With the codegen fix the end moves twice (parsing any_string, many1_chars, between_2 fail on cuda). Codegen and lib must change together: the lib edit (drop to_py and its unused trace helper) is staged as job tmp/rotation/patches/sm-prime-slice.after.spi and applied at pack install.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_4 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 4u32, "2026-10-14T18:25Z", "main-thread", "14:24 installed with pack-1d together with lib sm'.slice (Python +1 removed): ts_string_slice Python agrees with C in single-flight-20261014-140125 and its Known row is gone; the lib parsing/sm'/runtime/guid/crypto Python tests pass (lane B corpus check). Left: UTF-8 bytes vs code points.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_5 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 5u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: Python 22 rows, 20 agree, 1 known (pack-1h oracle). Still needs the upstream PR text.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_6 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 6u32, "2026-10-15T11:04Z", "main-thread", "07:04 decision (user 'we need all of them sota'): raised to P2; every backend stays on the active rotation.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_7 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 7u32, "2026-10-15T21:59Z", "main-thread", "17:59 Python coverage: probe single-flight-20261015-175614 (main): 402 rows agree with C; Python gets its own harness list (test.ps1 listed backends += Python) with 383 rows (<= 3 s), staged for pack-1n; 22 -> ~405 Python rows. 39 DISAGREE are the next Python targets.")
inl note_of_python_strings_upstream_8 () = Note ("PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM", 8u32, "2026-10-16T13:46Z", "main-thread", "09:46 main: pack-1u installed both modes (09:16/09:21) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-092123, 6,742 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells against the pack-1s bless 073131 overridden by probes 081908 (Kotlin), 082312 (Swift), 082906 (Bend), 084211 (Python). Harness Kotlin 444, Swift 443, Bend 401, Python 422.")
