inl note_of_wgsl_backend_5 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:59Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:59 lap 2 grain: dep choice from the bucket: of 481 C samples without a Wgsl row, union appears in 134 and array in 102 (string 247 is out of WGSL scope), so WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS/WGSL-PAYLOAD-UNIONS cover more rows than WGSL-STORAGE-ARRAYS Next: count samples whose only blockers are nullary unions (no payload) as the first union slice")
inl note_of_wgsl_backend_6 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 6u32, "2026-10-19T18:16Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:16 lap 4 grain: first union slice sized (accept 125623, C compile-ok samples without a Wgsl row, excluding strings, arrays, closures, heap, mut, 64-bit, recursive unions): 18 samples, 5 with nullary-only unions (match_multiline_scrutinee, nominal_union_case_pattern, op_args_application, tagged_union_enum, union_case_record_field_order) and 13 with scalar payloads (tagged_union_scalar, tagged_union_three_case, union_i8, union_call, qualified_union_case_pattern ...); so WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS buys 5 rows, and payload unions as a tag u32 + per-case scalar fields add 13 more Next: WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS: lower a nullary union to u32 constants and match to switch; prove with the 5 samples via a -Probe Wgsl candidate")
inl note_of_wgsl_backend_7 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 7u32, "2026-10-19T18:46Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:46 lap 5 grain: correction to lap 4: the union and array lowering already exists (codegenWgsl: tag-only unions are u32, payload unions a SpiralUnionN struct, arrays live in a spiral_heap buffer; WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS, WGSL-PAYLOAD-UNIONS and WGSL-STORAGE-ARRAYS are all Done), so what the item lacks is matrix rows; probe on the installed pack 7 compiler: 49 candidates compiled with --backend Wgsl, 35 compile, and all 35 run on spiral-wgsl (wgpu 30) with C exit codes (10 union samples + 25 ebpf_* scalar samples, empty stdout on both); the 14 failures are i8, heap layouts, closures (YFun) and 6 sample backend switches without a Wgsl arm. Staged lab/WGSL-BACKEND/add-proven.py (adds the 35 to the Wgsl list, dry run clean) for the pack after 8b Next: apply add-proven.py after pack 8b accepts, review (35 new Wgsl rows must agree), accept; AGENTS.md Wgsl paragraph still says unions and arrays are unsupported: fix the sentence with that pack")
inl note_of_wgsl_backend_8 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 8u32, "2026-10-19T21:20Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 17:20 main: pack 9 ACCEPTED 17:20 (single-flight-20261019-161549: 7,057 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells vs the Release candidate review 155055); the Wgsl list grew from 50 to 85 rows (10 union samples, 25 ebpf scalar samples), all agreeing with C; AGENTS.md Wgsl paragraph now describes the union and storage-array lowering.")
inl note_of_wgsl_backend_9 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 9u32, "2026-10-19T21:26Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 17:26 lap 5 grain: batch census (lab/BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS/blockers.ps1, one --batch compiler process, seconds instead of minutes) of the 413 C run-ok samples still without a Wgsl row on the pack 9 accept: strings 160, COMPILES 72, closures 38, sample backend switches without a Wgsl arm 38, layouts 21, f64 18, i64 18, recursive unions 14, sub-word 19; of the 72 that compile, 55 run on spiral-wgsl with C exit codes and empty stdout (staged in lab/BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS/wgsl-next.txt, dry run clean) and 17 fail WGSL validation (exit 2): non-tail recursion (frontier_fib, recur_sum, the managed_array scc samples, frontier_hopacsota_mutual_pending), C-ABI externs (abi_external*) and dynamic_array macros, a codegen bug, since codegenWgsl should raise its unsupported error for non-self-tail recursion instead of emitting a shader the validator rejects Next: add the 55 with the next pack; then make codegenWgsl detect non-self-tail recursion (a call to a join point on the current stack) and raise unsupported, proven by the 17 turning into compile errors")
inl note_of_wgsl_backend_10 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 10u32, "2026-10-19T21:35Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 17:35 lap 5 grain: recursion guard staged and proven on a private-cache Debug candidate: lab/WGSL-BACKEND/recursion_guard.py tracks the methods whose bodies are being emitted (method_memo registers the tag before emitting, so a recursive call sees it) and raises unsupported recursion that is not a self-tail call (WGSL has no call stack), the guard Calyx already has; the 5 recursive samples (frontier_fib, recur_sum, the two managed_array scc samples, frontier_hopacsota_mutual_pending) turn from invalid shaders into compile errors, all 85 listed Wgsl samples still compile, pair-drift clean (shared section); the other 12 invalid shaders come from C-only macro text in the samples (abi_external*, dynamic_array_* C shims), not codegen Next: pack 11: recursion_guard.py + the 55 staged rows (wgsl-next.txt), review, accept")
inl note_of_wgsl_backend_11 () = Note ("WGSL-BACKEND", 11u32, "2026-10-20T00:21Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 20:21 main: pack 11 ACCEPTED 20:21 (single-flight-20261019-191017: 7,276 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells vs the Release candidate review 190039); Wgsl list 85 -> 140 rows all agreeing (dynamic_array_bounds_negative on Wgsl is Known under the Zig oracle: robust buffer access reads unchecked like C); codegenWgsl now rejects non-self-tail recursion at compile time.")
