inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_16 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 16u32, "2026-10-15T03:01Z", "lane-b", "23:01 lane B: Hex rate-limit fix LANDED (uncommitted): apps/kino targets.ex gleam_build resolves once per dependency set under a :global lock and copies the locked manifest.toml from spiral-bin/kino-gleam-locks/<sha>.toml into every later gleam project (key = target + [dependencies], not the project name), toolchain.ex cache_dir public (opts :bin_cache_dir), targets_test lock-key test; Kino suite on a private copy with it: 235 tests, 5 failures, all environment artifacts of the copy (3 dice/alphabet siblings missing, private MIX_BUILD_PATH path assert, one slots timing assert under load), none in targets/memo/daemon tests")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_17 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 17u32, "2026-10-15T05:19Z", "lane-b", "01:19 lane B: correction: the landed gleam lock had a bug the copy suite did not reach: :global.trans got a 3-tuple id ({module, :gleam_resolve, path}) where it needs {resource, requester}, so every gleam build without a kept lock raised 'no function clause matching in :global.set_lock/4' (found by the pack-1g corpus check: 48 gleam-target tests failed in parsing/runtime/sm'/testing); fixed to {{Targets, :gleam_resolve, path}, self()} and covered by a new targets_test case that runs a real gleam build twice (first resolves under the lock and keeps the manifest, the second builds from it); targets_test 20/20")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_18 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 18u32, "2026-10-15T09:07Z", "lane-b", "05:07 lane B summary for the 21:31 push: eoie GREEN; spiral and .github red only on the gleam Hex rate limit (fixed in Kino, uncommitted, proven by the 1g corpus rerun 127/0 incl. every sm' gleam test and a real-gleam regression test); polyglot ubuntu green, windows runner lost; dice/alphabet not pushed (windows contract needs spiral_wasm in WSL, lands last); next: user commits Kino targets.ex/toolchain.ex, then read spiral/.github runs (windows jobs still lack evidence because fail-fast cancelled them)")
