inl multilingual_presentation () = Task ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", "One resolved program, several human presentations (Korean/Chinese/Hindi/Russian/Arabic and the original names): binding-aware alias tables that rename bindings only (never literals, JSON keys, FFI/external protocol names), checked by identical compile results; a pinned UAX #31 identifier profile with NFC for names only (string contents preserved); agents propose names and docs, tooling verifies; prototype mapping exists for the certificate sample (66 spellings, 4 presentations round-trip); 2026-10-14 02:32 lane 3 typed model (not compiled; C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\multilingual\\model.spi, 255 lines of Spiral unions/records + operation types), built from the geandra_v0_4.py prototype (per-locale bijective alias tables, NFC/identifier check, constructor marker for scripts without case, structural-AST equality after each translation): bindings are keyed by canonical name + kind (term, type, nominal, union case, record field, module, type variable, pattern variable, prototype, test name) + definition site, each with an exposure (internal or reaching JSON keys, foreign symbols, external protocol names, macro text, generated public names) and the fixed spellings that are never aliased (string and macro text, keywords per edition, symbols used as keys); alias tables per language profile (direction, letter case, constructor marking, Edition2Words or Edition3Symbols keywords, UAX #31 profile with NFC) are verified against one program digest; conflicts are a union: two aliases for one binding, one alias for two bindings in scope, shadowing and capture, keyword or edition-3-symbol clashes, non-NFC/non-UAX31, alias on a fixed spelling, unmarked constructor, unknown binding, table for another program; presentation maps presented spans to canonical source ranges, measures width in East Asian display columns for the formatter's 120 rule and reports overflow lines; edits map back to canonical patches or alias renames, and are rejected when the structure or residual hash changes; Zed/Kino/terminal/X surfaces carry display-only bidi isolates and a hover with the canonical name; 2026-10-14 02:34 lane 3 correction: model.spi is now 267 lines (not 255) after adding a surface_warning union on the presentation (bidi controls stripped, grapheme count differs from columns, hover unavailable, alias not renderable: the X-compat warnings), CanonicalNeedsAlphaRename (binding_key * edition) in round_trip_error for a canonical name that is a keyword in the other edition (the prototype's 'requires alpha-renaming before Spiral export'), and a separate resolve_failure for resolve_program; record-key decision: record field symbols are aliasable bindings (RecordFieldSymbol) unless a symbol reaches output as a key (SymbolLiteralUsedAsKey / ExposedBinding with JsonKey), which stays a fixed spelling", Epic, P3, D7, 0u32, Planned, "TEST-IDENTITY-I18N,SPIRAL3-EDITIONS", "i18n,edition,agents", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_multilingual_presentation () = Planning ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", Minutes 3000u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_1 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:46Z", "lane-a", "08:46 lane-a: width check for the formatter's 120 rule: 302 corpus lines are non-ASCII, 260 have display columns != UTF-16 length (lib 237), 0 change the over-120 verdict today. Decision: measure in East Asian display columns so presentations get the same limit. measure\\display-width.txt")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_2 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:49Z", "main-thread", "06:49 groom: unchanged; the formatter's 120-column rule still counts code points, not display width (302 non-ASCII corpus lines). P3.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_3 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom correction: the formatter does use display width where it matters. Layout.fsx fits (248) and Check.fsx (106) call Lexed.displayWidth (text elements). Only the over-120 tallies in Format.fsx (236, 247) use String.Length (UTF-16 units), so the reported counts can over-count non-ASCII lines. Next grain: switch those two tallies to displayWidth (lane A's files).")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_4 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 precision: String.Length differs from display width in both directions. Wide CJK characters count 1 but display 2, so it under-counts; combining sequences count several but display 1, so it over-counts. The tallies are approximate for non-ASCII lines; the layout itself is not affected.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_5 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 5u32, "2026-10-15T10:53Z", "main-thread", "06:53 groom: done for the tallies. Format.fsx over120-out, over120-out-outside-fences and the over120-left listing now use Lexed.displayWidth instead of String.Length (3 edits, LF). Smoke run on lib/spiral/sm'.spi (format, no --split-literals): exit 0 in 45 s, same counts as before on ASCII lines (3 long literals > 120, which --split-literals handles). So layout, checker and tallies all measure display width now. Remaining scope of this item: presentation of non-Latin identifiers and docs.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_6 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 6u32, "2026-10-17T19:02Z", "main-thread", "15:02 main-thread, user 2026-10-17 scope for edition 3: symbols plus presentations in each language's native writing, battle-testing edition 3: English (default), Portuguese, Chinese, Korean in hangul, Russian, Arabic, Spanish, French, Hindi, German, Japanese, Italian, Polish, Turkish. Goal: the canon programming term per function, code piece and notebook block in each culture's own developer jargon, not a literal gloss. Spend tokens once: a content-addressed translation cache keyed by (source text hash, language, translator id), so a name is translated once and every later run is a cache hit, like the compile memo. Benchmark the translators before choosing: a weak model, a SOTA model, and a dedicated MT system, scored by back-translation agreement, identifier validity (UAX 31 + NFC) and spot checks.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_7 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 7u32, "2026-10-17T19:02Z", "main-thread", "15:02 main-thread: English stays the default, and the translations feed back into picking it (user flagged this may be a stretch). A deterministic rule that fits the cache: for each candidate English name, take every cached round trip (English -> language -> English); the score is the number of languages whose round trip returns the same name. The highest score wins, ties go to the shorter name and then lexicographic order. Same cache, same choice; a new translator id invalidates only its own rows. Feeds LIB-CANON-NAMES.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_8 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 8u32, "2026-10-19T12:39Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:39 helper-lane lap 1: LAB-IN-REPO fix: the 10-14 typed model existed only in job tmp (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\multilingual\\model.spi, 268 lines, LF, comment-free: nominals for names/tags/digests, source_range, binding keys by kind, exposure, alias tables, conflict and round-trip unions). Copied it into the repo lab as spiral/lab/MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION/model.spi so it survives job-tmp cleanup and stays reviewable; the title's job-tmp path is now historical (original left in place). Deps unchanged: TEST-IDENTITY-I18N and SPIRAL3-EDITIONS.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_9 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 9u32, "2026-10-19T13:25Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:25 helper-lane lap 2: the rescued 10-14 model still type-checks on today's compiler: lab/MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION/model.spi as a module under a trivial probe_main.spi (try.ps1 C via Invoke-Heavy) compiles with exit 0, so its 268 lines of unions/records (binding keys, exposures, alias tables, conflicts, round-trip errors, surface warnings) are valid Spiral against the samples core after two weeks of compiler packs. That makes it usable as the typed spec when TEST-IDENTITY-I18N and SPIRAL3-EDITIONS open.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_10 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 10u32, "2026-10-19T14:57Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 10:57 helper-lane lap 3: first data instance of the model: lab/MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION/certificate_aliases.spi gives samples/contract_end_to_end_execution_certificate four alias tables (Korean, Chinese, Russian, Arabic) over its four user bindings, keyed by exact byte ranges in main.spi (certificate type 618-629, Certificate case 665-676, certify 924-931, render 1227-1233). Each table carries its language_profile: Korean, Chinese and Arabic are ScriptWithoutCase, so their constructors use ConstructorPrefixMark and the type and the case can share a spelling (인증서, 证书, شهادة) while Russian keeps UppercaseInitial (сертификат / Сертификат); Arabic is RightToLeft. Origin is AgentProposed, so check_alias_table must still verify them. Probe (try.ps1 C with model.spi + the table module, bounded): compiles, exit 16 = 4 tables x 4 entries, so non-Latin localized_name literals pass through the compiler and C intact.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_11 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 11u32, "2026-10-19T15:37Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:37 helper-lane lap 4: first check_alias_table rule as code, lab/MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION/check_rules.spi (unrun until main's freeze all-clear): two entries of one table that share a spelling are an OneAliasForTwoBindingsInScope conflict only when their bindings live in the same Spiral namespace (terms: term bindings, union case constructors, pattern variables, fields, prototypes; types: type, nominal and type-variable bindings; modules; test names). That is why the certificate tables' shared type/case spelling (인증서 for both certificate and Certificate) is legal: the type and the constructor are in different namespaces, so constructor marking is a readability rule, not a uniqueness one. Expected exit 1: the four certificate tables give 0 conflicts, and a Korean table that spells certify and render both 표시하다 gives exactly 1.")
inl note_of_multilingual_presentation_12 () = Note ("MULTILINGUAL-PRESENTATION", 12u32, "2026-10-19T17:42Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 13:42 helper-lane: probe run: check_rules.spi exits 1 as predicted - the four certificate tables have no same-namespace spelling conflict, and the Korean table spelling certify and render alike yields exactly one OneAliasForTwoBindingsInScope.")
inl query_cache_compiler () = Task ("QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER", "Persistent incremental compilation in the Hopac model, not a salsa-style query system (user decision 2026-10-13 23:34): results persisted per specialization key as hopacsota fill-once cells (parse per file, typecheck per package, specialization per join-point key, codegen per method), reused across builds when the key's inputs hash equal; return-type hints from the previous build feed D16.3 (checked, restart on a wrong guess); contract = lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md", Epic, P1, D8, 0u32, Planned, "HOPACSOTA-P2", "compiler,perf,cache", "current", "current")
