inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_4 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:35Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:35 lap 1 grain: unchanged since 10-15: grammar in apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, wiring waits for a commit rev (extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev) and the user's Zed check; nothing CPU-light left for agents beyond keeping the corpus test current Next: re-run the grammar's corpus parse over today's lib (401 test headers) to catch drift from new syntax (one light tree-sitter parse)")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_5 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:32 lap 2 grain, corrects lap 1 (wiring waits for a commit rev): apps/zed/extension.toml already pins [grammars.spiral] rev 3c76d3ed (2026-10-14 07:25), that commit is on github-i574n/main, its grammar.js has test_header, and git diff 3c76d3ed..HEAD over apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral is empty, so the pinned rev is the current grammar. Drift check without the tree-sitter CLI (not installed): the grammar is line-based and its test_header token is exactly ^test[ \\t]+ followed by a name of non-space non-= characters; over lib today that regex matches 402 lines in 40 files, the same 402 that ^test\\b matches (Grep count per file identical), so every compiler test header is a runnable and nothing new escapes it. Nothing CPU-light left for agents; what remains is the user's Zed check (ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES). Next: none for agents until the user reports the gutter check")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_6 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 6u32, "2026-10-19T15:23Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:23 lap 5 drift check widened from lib to every repo under C:\\home\\git: ^test\\b and the grammar's test_header shape ^test[ \\t]+[^ \\t=]+ both match 922 lines in the same 133 .spi/.spir files (lib, apps, lab, blog engine, dice, alphabet, eoie src, tibia, x, polyglot), so the pinned grammar rev 3c76d3ed still makes every test header in every consumer a runnable. Nothing else for agents; the user's Zed check stays (ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES, now incl. the worktree task gap).")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_7 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 7u32, "2026-10-19T15:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:40 lap 6 grain, the next grammar gap: outline.scm captures only test_header, because the grammar's definition_line is a single token (inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open/and plus the rest of the line) with no name field. Zed's outline panel and symbol search therefore list tests but none of the definitions (a lib file such as sm'.spi shows 42 tests and none of its functions). Proposed change: definition_line becomes seq(definition_keyword token, field name token.immediate([^\\s(:=]+), optional rest) at the same prec, and outline.scm gets (definition_line keyword @context name @name) @item, so definitions show up next to tests while the test headers stay exact. It needs tree-sitter generate (CLI not installed here), a grammar commit, and a new pinned rev in extension.toml, so it is the user's (or a CLI-equipped) step after the current gutter check.")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_8 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 8u32, "2026-10-19T16:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:40 lap 8 grain: the outline gap from lap 6 is staged as lab/TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL/definition_line.py (dry run by default; anchors ok): definition_line becomes seq(definition_keyword token at prec 2 that absorbs a leading and and a trailing rec, optional name field token.immediate of an identifier or a parenthesized operator such as (~#), optional definition_rest), the same shape as test_header; outline.scm gains a definition_line capture with keyword as context, skipping open via #not-match?; a corpus case covers open, inl rec, and inl, let, an operator and nominal. Regex check over lib: all 2,569 lines the current definition_line matches get a name under the new keyword+name pair, so no line falls into an error node. No query references definition_line today, so highlights are unaffected. Left: tree-sitter CLI (not installed) for generate + test, then a new grammar rev in extension.toml")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_9 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 9u32, "2026-10-19T17:15Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:16 lap 9 grain: definition_line.py proven with the real CLI on a scratch copy (npx tree-sitter-cli@0.25.10, the version of the committed parser.c, generate --abi 14). First run failed 2 of 4 corpus cases: the lexer preferred the longer definition_rest token over definition_name, and test_headers.txt still expected the old leaf definition_line. Fixed in the script: definition_name is token.immediate(prec(1, ...)) and the script rewrites that expectation (anchored once). Now: tree-sitter test 4/4, all 203 lib .spi/.spir files parse with 0 errors, outline query on am'_prototypes.spi yields item/context/name captures (array', a'). npm latest is 0.27.1 (ABI 15) = a separate bump after a Zed ABI check. Next: after the user's Zed check, definition_line.py --apply on apps/zed, generate --abi 14, test, new rev in extension.toml")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_10 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 10u32, "2026-10-19T17:41Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:41 lap 10 grain: definition_line.py now also appends highlights for the new nodes ((definition_keyword) @keyword, (definition_name) @function; guarded so it applies once). Rerun on a fresh scratch copy with tree-sitter-cli 0.25.10: generate --abi 14 ok, test 4/4, highlights/runnables/outline queries all run without query errors on lib testing.spi, and highlight captures go from 52 to 116 there (every inl/let/union/open line now colours its keyword and name; the outline keeps excluding open). Zed loads the grammar from extension.toml rev 3c76d3ed (on github-i574n/main, equal to the worktree grammar), so this change reaches Zed only through a commit + rev bump by the user. Next: user's Zed check, then --apply on apps/zed, generate, test, commit, rev bump")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_11 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 11u32, "2026-10-19T17:55Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:55 lap 11 grain, latest-of-everything for the grammar CLI: tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 (npm latest) generates the definition_line grammar with LANGUAGE_VERSION 15 and passes test 4/4 on a scratch copy; Zed main pins tree-sitter at git rev 43623ec (2026-08-20), 903 commits past v0.25.0, the release that introduced ABI 15, so Zed loads ABI 15 grammars. Decision for the apply step: regenerate with 0.27.1 (default ABI 15) instead of 0.25.10 --abi 14; the committed parser.c then moves from ABI 14 to 15 in the same rev bump. Next: after the user's Zed check, definition_line.py --apply, npx tree-sitter-cli@0.27.1 generate + test, commit, rev bump (user)")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_12 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 12u32, "2026-10-19T18:27Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 14:27 lap 12: corpus proof for definition_line.py on a scratch copy (cli 0.27.1, ABI 15): tree-sitter test 4/4, and parsing all 48 lib/spiral .spi files gives 1380 definition lines, every one with a definition_name, and 0 ERROR or MISSING nodes; the outline query on apps/cells console.spi lists the operator (~!\\\\), show_value, write_line and display. Ready to apply after the user's Zed check")
inl kino_source_diagnostics () = Task ("KINO-SOURCE-DIAGNOSTICS", "Found by xsim 2026-10-12: Kino diagnostics embed the per-request temp path (\".../Temp/spiral_kino/1791819891254-162/main.spi:10:8: Unbound variable ...\") so identical inputs give different text and the location points at a throwaway file; map diagnostics back to the source (.spi path + line, or cell index + line within the cell) so results are deterministic and clickable (Zed problem matcher); xsim normalizes the temp dir meanwhile; temp dir now stripped case-insensitively (either slash, optional file:///), messages read main.spi:10:8 and identical inputs give identical text (regression test); mapping main.spi lines back to the .spi line / cell is still open; 2026-10-13 12:25 done by the Kino lane: compile errors of .spi runs read <file>.spi:L:C (main.spi:L:C): Spiral.Kino.SourceMap matches the main.spi line to the source by its text (context lines break ties, column shifted by the indentation difference), ambiguous or unknown lines stay main.spi:L:C; tests in notebook_report_test.exs (real compile-error shape, ambiguity, context tie-break)", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,diagnostics,xsim", "current", "current")
