inl planning_of_tibia () = Planning ("TIBIA", Minutes 9600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_1 () = Note ("TIBIA", 1u32, "2026-10-15T01:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 21:14 NEXT AUTONOMOUS SESSION, in order (reprioritized after the 2026-10-14 harness fault and PR-4..PR-6): (1) TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY (P0): live lands ~67% of cyclops swings vs ~82% simulated; cadence and mitigation ruled out; measure the defense path (blocked swings per clear, needs a server-side log or a client build exposing effects), then model it and the queued drink during the 1 s potion exhaust; validate with a fresh pre-registered clear (not 3- or 2-cyclops rules, already seen). Until it holds, no simulator-designed policy goes live. (2) TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH (P1): second baseline; bisect _Loader.lua phases with the bot's own logging; then PR-3 as registered. (3) TIBIA-BASELINES: rules vs vBot was never pre-registered; consider PR-7 with the clean harness. Parked: TIBIA-PARTY, TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES, TIBIA-AGENT (stop rules reached; learning waits on fidelity). Rules: live blocks run alone (no Kino suites alongside), foreground chunks under 10 min, harness columns checked per block, final gate with SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0.")
inl note_of_tibia_2 () = Note ("TIBIA", 2u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: road so far: typed rules (24 modules, 69 tests, C+WGSL), local world, OTClient harness with parity, vBot and nExBot baselines, 8 pre-registered live checks. Roadmap order now: POTION-FIDELITY (P0) -> BASELINES -> RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD -> POLICY-FEATURES -> AGENT; headless client and release stay deferred.")
inl note_of_tibia_3 () = Note ("TIBIA", 3u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 PAUSED by the user: priority moves to dogfooding the tooling (eoie, backends, cells). Resume in a few weeks, aiming at GPU rental. State: rules level with vBot on a fair harness (PR-11); model mirrors live in-sample, misses on policy sensitivity (PR-10). Resume plan in order: TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY, TIBIA-START-SYNC, PR-12 (TIBIA-BASELINES), TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES, TIBIA-TOOLS-TO-EOIE, TIBIA-AGENT, TIBIA-GPU-RENTAL. Tooling items it waits on (generic): GPU-RENTAL-READINESS, EOIE-EXPERIMENTS, CELLS-REPIN, CELLS-GATE, CELLS-PROBES.")
inl note_of_tibia_4 () = Note ("TIBIA", 4u32, "2026-10-17T20:59Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:59 moved to its own repo (user): the 31 files of spiral/apps/tibia now sit at the root of C:\\home\\git\\tibia (origin github.com/i574n/tibia), hashes verified; docs' self-references fixed and spiral-tool paths prefixed spiral/. Verified from the new location, memo off: views 7, creatures 8, terrain 10, geometry 11, hunt_sim 11, gpu_sim 6 pass; live.spi compiles to the same Lua (7FD3D538...93E5). tibia-local run-arena.ps1 and run-policy-scenario.ps1 point at the new path. Titles and older notes that say apps/tibia refer to the old location.")
inl note_of_tibia_5 () = Note ("TIBIA", 5u32, "2026-10-17T21:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 17:54 repo completed sibling-style (user: the first move was sloppy): AGPL LICENSE, .editorconfig/.gitattributes/.gitignore/.devcontainer like alphabet; scripts/init.ps1 (clones polyglot, links deps/polyglot + deps/spiral, mesa-vulkan-drivers on Ubuntu, builds the WGSL runner into target/), build.ps1 (every test file through cells, fails unless all rows executed and passed), publish.ps1, workflow.ps1; .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml (Ubuntu + Windows, gh-pages push on main) with gh actions-lock. Harness moved from tibia-local into harness/ (paths.ps1: repo vs TIBIA_WORLD), results/ holds the cited TSVs and diagnostics; tibia-local keeps the world only (originals archived in job tmp). i574n.github init/build/workspace register tibia next to dice and alphabet. Verified locally: init -fast ok, build.ps1 23 files / 162 tests green (12 min), live smoke from harness/ cleared (82.8 s, 0 foreign). CI not run yet: needs the user's push. nExBot stays out of the repo (no license).")
inl note_of_tibia_6 () = Note ("TIBIA", 6u32, "2026-10-17T23:05Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 19:05 repo root slimmed (user): the Spiral package moved to src/ (package.spiproj + 24 modules), the five design docs to docs/; README, scripts/build.ps1 (src/*.spi; -Files now splits on commas), harness/paths.ps1 (TibiaSource) and the arena snapshot follow. Verified: build.ps1 -Files views,creatures green from src/, live.spi from src/ compiles to the same Lua (7FD3D538...), snapshot copy 25 files. Rewrite plan for the non-Spiral code: TIBIA-PROBES-IN-SPIRAL (Lua probes, biggest gain), TIBIA-TOOLS-TO-EOIE (analyses and orchestration onto generic eoie verbs), TIBIA-MAP-TOOL-IN-SPIRAL (Python map tool); apps/arena and apps/map folders come with those rewrites.")
inl note_of_tibia_7 () = Note ("TIBIA", 7u32, "2026-10-18T06:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 02:54 ACTIVE again (user correction: Tibia is not paused; advance everything until it is good enough to start Dota 2). Order: finish TIBIA-PROBES-IN-SPIRAL; TIBIA-WGSL-SHADER-SIZE (decide by experiment) and TIBIA-WINDOWS-CI-GPU (lavapipe on Windows); TIBIA-REUSE-EXEMPLAR; then CELLS-NEW-PROJECT, then Dota 2. Repo layout now: src/ (package), docs/, live/ (renamed from harness/ by session git-0e), results/, apps/arena/ (probes in Spiral), scripts/, CI on both OSes (Ubuntu green; Windows fails only the 4 long GPU twins). The user commits and pushes.")
inl note_of_tibia_8 () = Note ("TIBIA", 8u32, "2026-10-18T11:21Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 07:21 session summary toward 'good enough for Dota 2'. Done: TIBIA-PROBES-IN-SPIRAL (all 9 live probes are Spiral, no probe Lua left; lua.spi has tests), TIBIA-WGSL-SHADER-SIZE (inline everything, let start: 3.63 -> 2.36 MB, cold driver compile 167 -> 68 s; every extra let measured slower). Active: TIBIA-WINDOWS-CI-GPU 80% (lavapipe + LunarG loader on Windows CI, DXC as local fallback; waits for the spiral runner commit and a tibia push), TIBIA-REUSE-EXEMPLAR 40% (lua.spi / client.spi / probe.spi layering is the Dota template), TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY 85% (first swing folded into the mirror; over-count analysed: no single mechanism, needs clean runs). New: DOTA epic with DOTA-HEADLESS-WORLD, DOTA-LUA-BINDINGS, DOTA-FIRST-SCENARIO; CELLS-EXPORT-ATOMIC-WRITE. Compiler lane fixed SPIRAL-LUA-CLOSURE-RECORD-ARG and SPIRAL-LUA-PAREN-STATEMENT (verified here). Remaining before Dota: CELLS-NEW-PROJECT (its deps are cells/eoie items), green CI on both OSes after the pushes, renting the CPU box.")
inl tibia_local_world () = Task ("TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "Local world, all prebuilt: Canary 3.6.1 (opentibiabr/canary 2026-07-01, canary-windows-cmake-release.zip, map otservbr.otbm, GPL-2.0) + OTClient Redemption 4.1 (opentibiabr/otclient 2026-08-15, otclient-windows-solution-opengl.zip) + MariaDB + the official 15.x client assets the client needs; exit: log in, walk, kill a creature; keep binaries outside the repos; 2026-10-13 06:14 exit met: log in and walk (2026-10-12) and a verified kill (skeleton, experience +52, 2026-10-13) through tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA", "tibia,server", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_local_world () = Planning ("TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl tibia_typed_rules () = Task ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", "Hunt subset of Canary's rules as Spiral modules in the apps/tibia package (grid and floors, creatures melee/ranged/flee, cooldown groups, HP/mana, potions, loot, death penalty); integer-only so CPU and WGSL traces are bit-identical; started 2026-10-12, all passing through run_notebook: geometry.spi (8 incl. prelude), vitality.spi (5, GADT typestate living/fallen), coins.spi (5, gold/platinum/crystal conservation), rng.spi (6, counter-based lowbias32 keyed by seed/tick/entity/purpose, reference values from an independent implementation), cooldowns.spi (6, spell groups plus own cooldown), hunt.spi (4, uses other modules via ///- --package .), hunt_sim.spi (6, deterministic 600-tick hunt, golden seed 7 = 7 kills/140 gold/69 health); every rules test lists ///> rust and ///> c (40 tests, 0 failures, 489 s full run 2026-10-12)", Feature, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA,TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC", "tibia,spiral,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_typed_rules () = Planning ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", Minutes 1800u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: status was stale (Planned 0%). Verified now: 24 .spi modules in apps/tibia, 69 tests pass memo off on pack-1h (06:15). Left from the original list: loot conservation tests, death penalty, ranged creatures.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 2u32, "2026-10-18T17:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 13:33 loot conservation done: hunt.spi test loot_conserves_gold_and_pays_in_fewest_coins_over_1600_purses_and_bounties (C oracle) loops 1600 purses (gold, platinum, up to 6 crystal) against bounties 0..996. A kill must add exactly the bounty to the purse's gold value and pay it back in fewest coins (gold and platinum each under 100); a survivor must leave the purse value unchanged. Result: 0 broken, hunt 5/5 through scripts/build.ps1. Left from the original list: death penalty (level and skill loss, gear drop without blessings, both seen live) and ranged creatures (no arena creature uses ranged attacks yet).")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 3u32, "2026-10-18T17:36Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 13:36 death penalty, experience part: new module src/experience.spi (registered in package.spiproj after vitality). experience_for_level is Canary's Player::getExpForLevel ((((L-6)L+17)L-12)/6*100). unblessed_death_loss_below_level_24 = experience / 10, Canary's getLostPercent for level < 24, no blessings, unpromoted, deathLosePercent -1 as in tibia-local config.lua; floor(experience * 0.1) in double equals experience / 10 for every integer. after_unblessed_death applies the loss and Canary's level-down loop (while level > 1 and experience < experience_for_level level). Tests: the exp table against the formula (levels 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 10, 24, 100), Knight Sample level 8 at 4200 dies to level 7 at 3780 (the live 'deaths cost a level'), a mid-level death that keeps its level, and a WGSL twin; experience 4/4. Left: skill-try loss (needs vocation skill-try tables), the level >= 24 double formula, gear drop without blessings, and ranged creatures.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 4u32, "2026-10-18T18:23Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 14:23 three more rules, all from Canary source and data, C oracle + WGSL twin, gate green. (1) experience.spi fix: the loss is ceil(experience * 0.1) (player.cpp 4031), which equals (experience + 9) / 10 for every experience up to 50,000,000 (checked exhaustively); vocations at level <= 7 lose no experience (level > 7 guard); tests now include 4205 -> 3784 (level 7) and level 7 kept (experience 5/5). (2) skills.spi: knight_skill_tries_up_to_130 is Canary's getReqSkillTries table, uint64(50 * pow((double)1.1f, level - 11)), generated as a binary-search let chain like terrain's masks. The fractional parts never come within 1.2e-6 of an integer, so libm differences cannot flip it. after_unblessed_death is Canary's skill loss loop (sum of tries / 10, walking levels down, floor at 10). Pinned against a C# replica of the loop: axe 30 with 0 tries -> 29 with 20 tries (the live 'a skill point'), 60/1234 -> 59/629, 11/0 -> 10/45, 130/0 -> 128/3409614; skills 4/4. (3) blessings.spi: Blessings.DropLoot from data/libs/systems/blessing.lua: per slot, a container drops at chance x 100 out of 10000, any other item at a tenth of that; 0 blessings: backpack always and each other item 1000/10000; blessing table 70/45/25/10/0; Amulet of Loss none; red or black skull everything (blessings 3/3). (4) combat.spi: ranged attacks (hunter arrow from data-canary hunter.lua: 50% every 2000 ms, 0..100 physical, range 7). Canary's distance spells set BLOCKARMOR but not BLOCKSHIELD, so arrows skip the shield, yet blockHit still spends a block charge because it decrements whenever armor or defense is checked; pinned over 4000 arrows (equal to an unshielded melee roll, one charge spent each, 0 stays 0); reach needs distance <= 7 and clear sight (Monster::canUseAttack); combat 9/9. Left: wiring a ranged creature into the simulator (keep-distance movement from Monster::getDistanceStep) and the level >= 24 death formula.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 5u32, "2026-10-18T18:46Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 14:46 ranged creature wired into the simulator (uncommitted; existing camps unaffected, gate running): creatures.Hunter (data-canary hunter.lua: 150 hp, speed 105, step 600 ms, targetDistance 4, melee 0..20, armor/defense 15, runHealth 10) with is_ranged / ranged_attack_of; creatures.spi gained its missing '///- --package .' line (it now needs combat). hunting_pack: a ranged foe keeps its target distance (steps away with terrain.step_away while closer and in sight) and every 2000 ms gets an attack round: melee if adjacent, plus an arrow roll when in range 7 with clear sight (geometry.sight_line_clear over the layout's walls); the arrow uses combat.ranged_hit_spending_a_charge. Finding from a probe (lab/tibia-potion-fidelity/hunter_chase_probe.spi): on the unbounded open field the level-8 knight (~700 ms per tile) never catches a hunter (600 ms steps), which re-opens to 4 tiles whenever the knight reaches 3; 60 s: 0 kills, 28 arrow hits, 28 potions. On ArenaSpot the knight reaches a hunter but gets no kill in 60 s, then the run resets. Not pinned: how fast a live knight catches hunters, and the dance and cornering from Monster::getDistanceStep, need a live reference first (exploratory hunter runs planned in today's live block).")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 6u32, "2026-10-18T19:27Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:27 WGSL cost of the ranged wiring, measured on gpu_sim (local NVIDIA, cold): with the ranged branch compiled into every simulator shader, the three shaders grew from 1.25/2.36/1.41 MB (this morning's CI) to 1.52/2.90/1.69 MB, and the largest's cold compile went to 124 s. Fix: a camp-level static flag (camp.ranged, set by uniform_camp / the mixed-camp builder / the hunting-ground camp from creatures.is_ranged) gates both ranged branches. For camps built from literal kinds, Spiral folds it away, and the shaders are back to 1.26/2.38/1.42 MB (largest compiles in 80 s); gpu_sim 6/6. Same lesson as TIBIA-WGSL-SHADER-SIZE: a rule only some scenarios use should hang off a static camp property, so GPU shaders of other scenarios don't pay for it.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 7u32, "2026-10-18T19:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:32 source for the hunter-chase gap: Monster::getDistanceStep keeps a counter (monster.cpp 1748-1755): when the target is within 1 tile on both axes, stepDuration++ (max 2), otherwise stepDuration-- (min 0). Monster::isTargetNearby() is stepDuration >= 1, and Creature::getStepDuration multiplies a straight step by WALK_TARGET_NEARBY_EXTRA_COST = 2 while the monster is not fleeing and not a summon (diagonals pay WALK_DIAGONAL_EXTRA_COST = 3 instead). So a hunter the knight has reached steps at about 1200 ms and can be held, while the model's hunter keeps 600 ms and escapes. Melee monsters return before the counter (distance == targetDistance), which matches the live cyclops 'no x2 after contact'. Next: a per-foe nearby counter (0..2) updated at each ranged step decision, doubling the straight step cost while >= 1, behind the static camp.ranged flag.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 8u32, "2026-10-18T20:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 16:54 ranged creature rule completed in the model: (1) Canary's keep-distance slow-down (Monster::getDistanceStep counts 'target within 1 tile' up to 2, down to 0; while >= 1 a straight step costs x2, WALK_TARGET_NEARBY_EXTRA_COST; diagonal x3 as always; only in the keep-distance branch, which is why melee cyclops chase steps show no x2 live) as foe field nearby + target_nearby_step_factor. (2) bug found by the lab probe: hardest_kind treated only Cyclops as tough, so a hunter camp fell back to the Troll offense (level 8, axe 30, 30-60 hp potions) and the new Hunter offense row was dead; hardest_kind now picks the camp kind with the highest offense level from offense_against itself, so the table and the picker cannot drift again (all other camps get the same offense as before). Pinned: pack_sim a_hunter_that_keeps_four_tiles_away_only_falls_where_walls_corner_it_and_walking_next_to_the_knight_halves_its_pace (5 seeds x 120 s, 3 hunters: open field 0 kills / 286 hits taken, arena spot 15 kills (all) / 121 hits). Lab: lab/tibia-potion-fidelity hunter_chase_probe.spi, hunter_adjacency_probe.spi. Model-only claim, no live hunter runs yet.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_rules_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", 9u32, "2026-10-18T21:17Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 17:17 gates green after the hunter rule and the hardest_kind fix: pack_sim 30/30 (every earlier pin unchanged), creatures 8/8, hunt_sim 11/11, gpu_sim 6/6. WGSL cost: shaders 1.26/2.38/1.42 MB -> 1.30/2.47/1.47 MB (+3.5%), most likely the foe record's new nearby field, which every foe copy carries even though its logic sits behind camp.ranged; the largest compiled cold in 94 s vs 80 s, measured while the compiler lane's heavy gate ran, so not comparable. Accepted. Scope of the title is covered: grid and floors (up_ramp), creatures melee/ranged/flee, cooldown groups, HP/mana, potions, loot (blessing drops), death penalty (experience, skills, gear). Live validation of the ranged rules continues as PR-13 under TIBIA-FIDELITY.")
inl tibia_fidelity () = Task ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", "Diff the simulator against Canary as the oracle: deterministic mechanics bit-exact, RNG mechanics through a seeded local Canary build or distribution tests of its damage/loot formulas; one verdict per mechanic, every gap named", Feature, P2, D6, 65u32, Active, "TIBIA-TYPED-RULES,TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,oracle", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_fidelity () = Planning ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", Minutes 1800u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: status was stale (Planned 0%). Verdicts so far: walk steps pinned; step timing and road speed hold (PC-1, PC-2); monster wake holds; melee hit distribution holds (33.6 vs 34.97); swing delay after a step holds (PC-3); potion use still off for retreat (POTION-FIDELITY).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 2u32, "2026-10-18T19:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:28 verdicts added 2026-10-18, each against Canary 3.6.1 source or data-canary: floor change onto an up-ramp holds (geometry.climbed, the live 1940,1372,7 -> 1940,1373,6 pinned); death experience loss is formula-equal (ceil(e*0.1) = (e+9)/10 exhaustive to 50M, level <= 7 spared), live 'loses a level' reproduced; death skill loss is formula-equal (getReqSkillTries table plus the loss loop, against a C# replica), live 'a skill point' reproduced; gear drop is formula-equal (blessing.lua DropLoot), not yet measured live; line of sight is bit-exact (Map::checkSightLine port, against a C# replica); block charges match source (refill per think, zero rolls spend charges, distance spells spend a charge without shield defense); post-step swing: the model has Canary's onCreatureMove resumption (the attack-command path does not apply to our probe, because OTClient's attack toggles); ranged hunters: formulas typed, behavior (keep-distance and cornering) unverified and in gap. Open gaps: potion use (POTION-FIDELITY, damage per landed hit 35.2 live vs 36.5 model), ranged-monster movement, and the RNG mechanics' seeded oracle (ORACLE-RNG).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 3u32, "2026-10-18T21:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 17:04 PR-13 pre-registered in docs/BENCHMARK.md before any hunter run: 3 hunters on the arena spot, spiral-policy (rules heal 160), 10 runs; model prediction 2.67 potions (sd 1.89), 63.6 s with the 200 s cap, 99/100 clear; holds if both one-sample t within 2.26 and 9+/10 clear. First live test of the ranged rules (keep-distance slow-down, checkSightLine port, arrows skip the shield). Live slot granted by the compiler lane after its core compile census tonight.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 4u32, "2026-10-19T01:51Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 21:51 PR-13 (ranged hunters on the arena spot, pre-registered 17:04) FAILS on its clear-rate rule: 5 of 10 live runs clear against the model's 99 of 100. Potions t 0.40 (3.00 per run vs 2.67); clear time t -0.40 over the 5 clears (61.6 s vs 63.6). No deaths; health conservation 44/44. Uncleared runs end at the 200 s cap with 225 or 450 experience. The log shows the knight targeting a hunter for about 1,000 ticks with no strike, so live hunters escape reach more often than the model's keep-distance slow-down allows. Next: compare the hunter's live step pattern (positions every tick from the probe) with Monster::getDistanceStep and the arena geometry, then fix the model and pre-register PR-14. Results in results/arena-results-hunter-pr13.tsv, logs in tibia-local/arena-logs 20261018-21*-hunter-*. pr2-analysis.ps1 prints 'predicts' because it only checks the two t values.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 5u32, "2026-10-19T06:39Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 02:39 Correction to the PR-13 note: the uncleared runs do not keep a hunter targeted with no strike. They log 'attacking nothing'. All five uncleared runs (1, 2, 4, 6, 9) make their last kill far east (x 1942-1957) after chasing a fleeing hunter along y 1352-1354, and the other two hunters never come back into the client's view. The cleared runs kill at x 1920-1937. Model side (lab/tibia-fidelity, hunter_stall_probe.spi and hunter_companions_probe.spi, outputs saved next to them): the model knight also ends up to 22 tiles east and 21 north, yet clears 100/100, because the remaining hunters shadow it at about 4 tiles (keep-distance approach while within the 11x11 view). Canary's MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT_X/Y = 11/11 matches the model's view, and the Hunter stats (speed 105, targetDistance 4, runHealth 10, staticAttackChance 90) match creatures.spi. So the gap is in how live companions follow. Next: apps/arena now logs a 'seen at x,y: <monster hp% x,y; ...>' line every 10 ticks (competitor.spi, client.monsters_described, scoreboard.due_for_trace); a 5-run diagnostic block (not pre-registered) in main's slot around 03:15-03:30 will show what the companions do.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 6u32, "2026-10-19T09:27Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 05:27 diagnostic block (5 runs, 05:02-05:14, not pre-registered): 4/5 clear (9/15 with PR-13). Uncleared run: knight drags a fleeing hunter 30 tiles east, third hunter falls behind at 5 tiles, leaves view, knight idles to the cap. Live follow pace beyond 4 tiles 0.83-0.93 tiles/s vs model 1.15-1.19 (lab/tibia-fidelity/follow-pace.ps1 on live and model seen-at traces). Model change: ranged hunter beyond target distance steps only on its creature think (hunting_pack.thinks_now) -> model pace 0.91-1.00, 94/100 held-out clears (was 100), stranding reproduced. Canary cause not pinned (path re-plans on every knight move; A* start node satisfies at target distance). Remaining gap 94% vs 60% live. pack_sim test updated (hits 286->173 open, 121->135 arena; kills unchanged) + new test a_hunter_beyond_four_tiles_closes_one_tile_per_think. BENCHMARK PR-13 diagnostic row. Next: find the remaining live stall (walk-back on empty screen, monster idle when no player on screen) before pre-registering PR-14.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 7u32, "2026-10-19T10:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:00 Canary source checks for the residual hunter gap (local canary/src): view is MAP_MAX_VIEW_PORT 11x11 (map_const.hpp, matches model); follow re-plans on every followed-creature move (creature.cpp onCreatureMove isUpdatingPath + updateCreatureWalk, async pathfinder) plus every 2 s on think (walkUpdateTicks); A* start node already at target distance returns a path (map.cpp getPathMatchingCond), so hasFollowPath stays true; hunter speed 105 (data-canary hunter.lua) = 600 ms. None explains the slower live pace, so thinks_now stays a calibration. Model gap found: a monster whose target list empties walks back to its spawn (monster.cpp updateIdleStatus -> isWalkingBack, doWalkBack until a player is on screen), the model stands still; same stranding outcome, matters only if the knight returns. Residual 94% vs 60% needs more traced live runs: only 1 of 15 uncleared-capable runs had the trace. Next live slot: trace-on PR-14 pre-registered on the calibrated model.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 8u32, "2026-10-19T10:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:02 PR-14 pre-registered in docs/BENCHMARK.md (before any run): hunter clear on the calibrated model, 10 traced live runs into results/arena-results-hunter-pr14.tsv. Prediction (lab/tibia-fidelity/hunter_pr14_prediction_probe.spi, 100 held-out, 200 s cap): 94/100 clear, 2.36 potions (sd 1.51), 62.0 s per clear (sd 11.8), 15.9 hits, 0 deaths. Holds at >=9/10 clears and both t within 2.26; fails at <=7 clears (P=0.019 under 0.94) or a t beyond; 8 inconclusive. Alternative: pre-rule model 100/100.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 9u32, "2026-10-19T10:29Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:29 PR-14 RESULT (06:03-06:28, 10 runs, results/arena-results-hunter-pr14.tsv): FAILS on clear rate, 7/10 (pre-registered fail at <=7). Potions 4.10 (t 2.15) and clear time 60.4 s (t -0.31) within. Follow-pace rule holds live (1.00/0.91 tiles/s at gap 5/6 vs model 0.91/1.00). New finding: over 15 traced runs all 4 uncleared reach knight x 1960-1967, all 11 cleared stay <=1953. Model arena spot is radius 30 (terrain.arena_spot_radius, wall at x 1963 = model 130), so fleeing hunters get cornered at the window edge in the model while live the road continues east. Next: widen the scanned spot in apps/map (needs more than two u32 words per row), rerun the probes and the cyclops tests, then a new pre-registration.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 10u32, "2026-10-19T10:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:31 Confirmed the window cut: a lab copy of apps/map with spot_radius 45 (lab/tibia-fidelity/map-wide, walkability-radius-45.txt) shows walkable ground continuing east of x 1963 (rows y 1351-1353 and 1356-1360 open well past it); live tiles 1963,1352 / 1964,1352 / 1967,1334 read walkable. The model's radius-30 window walls this off. Fix path: raise arena_spot_radius past 45 in apps/map (rows need 3 u32 words), regenerate terrain tables, rerun the 251/252 live scan check and the cyclops pack_sim tests, re-predict, then pre-register PR-15.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY", 11u32, "2026-10-19T10:32Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 06:32 Scope for the wider spot (read-only check): apps/map/map.spi row_words packs a row into a (low, high) u32 pair (low_word_bits 32), so spot_radius tops out at 31; terrain.spi reads the pair at arena_spot_low/high, arena_road_low/high, region_high_bits and the region router (lines 106-142, open_low/open_high, marked_low/high). Plan: a typed row of two u64 words (radius up to 63) in both files, radius about 45, regenerate with apps/map/run.ps1 -Update. The lab map-wide radius-45 tables wrap past 64 columns; only its readable grid dump is valid evidence.")
inl tibia_baselines () = Task ("TIBIA-BASELINES", "Arena baselines on a frozen scenario pack: headless protocol client (Spiral/Rust), nExBot (github.com/mCodex/nExBot, pushed 2026-09-01, no license file detected: confirm), vBot (OTClient Redemption 4.1 ships mods/game_bot with default_configs/vBot_4.8 and cavebot_1.3, so it runs on Canary's protocol 1511; also in OTCv8/otclientv8, which stops at 11.x), a scripted cavebot, a random-policy control; parity rules (15x11 view, one action-rate cap, same character/supplies/seeds); real-time evaluation budget ~150 h of play per pass at 2-3 client+server pairs; 2026-10-13 07:46 first baseline live: vBot_4.8 (OTClient Redemption's mods/game_bot) runs headless-configured through tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1 -Bot vBot (fresh copy of the shipped config, TargetBot config vbot-arena.json: troll, chase, priority 1; storage enables it; probe-vbot-body.lua only enables the bot through g_settings and observes); 3 trolls, balanced, axe 30: vBot +90 experience (3 kills) in ~105 s, lowest health 181; the Spiral policy (CurrentFirst) +90 (3 kills) in ~103 s, lowest 178: a tie on this small scenario; next: the parity layer (action-rate cap, 15x11 view) and harder scenarios (cyclops, mixed packs) with seeds; 2026-10-13 08:44 parity layer live (tibia-local/parity.lua, prepended to every probe unless -NoParity): one shared gate admits at most one action per 250 ms across g_game attack/follow/walk/turn/talk/use*/move/cancel* and LocalPlayer.autoWalk, and g_map.getSpectators returns only creatures within the 15x11 client screen; 3 trolls under parity: vBot +90 experience in ~80 s (17 actions allowed, 7 dropped), Spiral policy +90 in ~90 s (16 allowed, 5 dropped); next: repeated seeds per competitor and harder scenarios (vBot needs HealBot configured for anything dangerous); 2026-10-13 09:26 first repeated arena table (tibia-local/run-arena.ps1, 5 alternating runs each, 3 trolls, parity on, policy compiled from a snapshot; arena-results.tsv): full clears Spiral 4/5 (mean 92.1 s over full clears, actions 15.2), vBot 5/5 (mean 108.0 s, sd 21.7, actions 22.8); Spiral's missed clear came from its own stop rule (no visible target) when a fleeing troll left the 15x11 parity view; the stop rule is now full experience for both; no significant difference at n=5; next: more runs, the harder cyclops scenario (vBot needs HealBot); 2026-10-13 10:06 cyclops arena live layer: run-policy-scenario.ps1 gains -Level (experience, max health 185+15(L-8), mana derived), -HealBelow/-StrikeAbove (TIBIA_ARENA_HEAL_BELOW/STRIKE_ABOVE read by both probe bodies, troll defaults unchanged), potion 266 restocked to 100 in the reset, vBot TargetBot regex from -Monster and a seeded HealBot.json (potion 266 below the same hp threshold, profiles 0 and 1); run-arena.ps1 passes them through, sets the full-experience stop rule, and keeps every run's full output in tibia-local/arena-logs; smoke round (level 30, axe 60, 3 cyclops, heal below 150): BOTH competitors died within 10 s of the summon (vBot log: dead before t=10s, 7 actions), while the simulator's same knight survives most 5-minute hunts; potion (125-175) and cyclops melee (0-105 per 2 s) match Canary's scripts, so the gap is elsewhere (heals not landing live, or extra damage); diagnosis run was reaped for low memory at 10:05, retry after the compiler chain frees memory; 2026-10-13 10:17 cyclops smoke deaths explained: (1) no potions: deaths in earlier runs dropped the backpack's contents and the reset only updated an existing row, so the 'Sorry, not possible' heal had nothing to drink; the reset now deletes and re-inserts 100 potions in the backpack (verified live: 'Using one of 100 health potions', heals 141-170); (2) the probe marked a heal done even when the parity gate dropped it; it now retries next tick; (3) a cyclops kill gives 225 experience on this server (rate stage), so three cyclops need -FullExperience 675; 2026-10-13 12:19 cyclops clear arena v1 (BENCHMARK pack v1 'cyclops clear', forge off, heal below 70 for all, tibia-local/arena-results-cyclops.tsv since 11:35, arena-summary.ps1): kiting network 4/5 cleared, 85.5 +- 8.2 s, 13.6 +- 4.4 potions, 2425 +- 634 damage; rules 4/5, 92.7 +- 15.2 s, 14.2 +- 1.9, 2506 +- 232; vBot 3/4, 90.0 +- 17.3 s, 12.0 +- 6.9; every competitor died once; no significant separation at n=4-5 (the first-run kiting gain was noise); heal 70 is unsafe live, which the simulator missed (fixed since: Canary block charges, diagonal x3 and chase x2 steps, the 250 ms action gap as a typed readiness witness, live spawn layout); live layer fixes during v1: vBot HealBot Visible=false, vBot probe logs damage, -Competitors parsing; v2 next: probe retreats only onto walkable tiles (live kiting walked into walls), threshold re-tuned on the corrected simulator; 2026-10-13 13:39 cyclops clear arena v2 (heal below 100 for all, probe v2 with walkable retreats, arena-results-cyclops-v2.tsv): vBot 5/5 cleared, 0 deaths, 88.0 +- 11.0 s, 15.8 +- 4.3 potions; rules 4/5, 1 death (that run also had the parity gate reporting admitted potions as dropped, fixed 13:12), 86.6 +- 4.9 s, 14.2 +- 6.5; kiting 2/5, 3 deaths (the simulator also ranks it worst; the arena spot is walled in, 38 of 39 retreat decisions found no walkable tile); live layer asymmetry found: vBot's HealBot macro runs every 100 ms while our probe decided every 250 ms, both behind the same 250 ms action gate, so vBot reacted faster to bursts; the probe now ticks every 100 ms like vBot (the gate still caps actions), and clear time is measured in ms by both probes; v3 next: rules vs vBot only; 2026-10-13 14:16 cyclops clear arena v3 (first with matched decision rates: our probe ticks every 100 ms like vBot's HealBot macro, same 250 ms action gate, heal below 100 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v3.tsv): Spiral rules 4/5 cleared, 80.1 +- 7.0 s, 13.4 +- 6.3 potions, 2369 +- 871 damage, 1 death; vBot 4/5, 90.0 +- 11.5 s, 13.8 +- 6.3, 2461 +- 882, 1 death; clear-time difference not significant (Welch t = -1.47, n = 4 each); next: 10+ runs per competitor before claiming a gap, and the simulator's learned policies once they dominate by more than noise; 2026-10-13 14:46 ARENA DATA INVALIDATED after 12:02: deaths dropped the knight's equipment (no blessings) and the reset restored only potions, so from the first death on the knight fought with less gear (clean runs: 33.6 mean per landed hit, max 86; afterwards 38-45, max up to 101; by 14:27 helmet, armor, legs, shield and backpack were all gone and every run died with 0 potions); v1 rows after 12:02, all of v2 and v3 are void (files renamed *-gear-lost-invalid); the reset now deletes the knight's items and inserts the canonical set (brass helmet, backpack, brass armor, dwarven shield, steel axe, brass legs, leather boots, store inbox, 100 potions); also void: the 'live mean 37.6 over 794 hits' used as evidence for block charges; block charges stay as Canary's mechanic, but the clean data (33.6) sits closer to always-blocked; 2026-10-13 15:26 cyclops clear arena v4, the first clean comparison (full inventory restored before every run, forge off, same 250 ms action gate and 100 ms decision tick, heal below 160 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v4.tsv): Spiral rules 6/6 cleared, 87.9 +- 14.3 s, 14.7 +- 2.9 potions, 2471 +- 420 damage, 0 deaths; vBot 6/6, 90.0 +- 8.9 s, 14.8 +- 2.6 potions, 2486 +- 395, 0 deaths; a tie (Welch t -0.31 on time, -0.10 on potions), as the simulator expects for two threshold healers; next: the arena spot's terrain in the simulator, then a scenario where terrain or positioning separates policies; 2026-10-13 16:33 arena v5 (clean, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v5.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst) 7/7 cleared, 83.3 +- 6.3 s, 12.1 +- 2.8 potions, 2101 +- 432 damage; vBot 6/6, 83.4 +- 15.1 s, 13.0 +- 3.1, 2201 +- 469; Spiral rules 6/6, 83.1 +- 11.0 s, 14.2 +- 2.2, 2376 +- 337; no deaths; retreat uses the fewest potions at equal time, the simulator's direction, but smaller than predicted (-15% vs rules live, -33% in the simulator) and not yet significant (Welch t -1.45 vs rules, -0.52 vs vBot); 10 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 18:25 arena v5 final (16/16/15 runs, clean): Spiral retreat-at-2 13.8 +- 2.9 potions, 88.9 +- 9.9 s; vBot 14.1 +- 2.5, 88.0 +- 10.8 s; Spiral rules 14.4 +- 2.6, 86.8 +- 12.4 s; no deaths; no significant differences (retreat vs rules t -0.58); the early retreat advantage regressed to the mean; the simulator's ~30% saving does not transfer; live retreats mostly did not move the knight (sampled positions barely change): the probe left ChaseOpponent on, so the server walked the knight back toward its target; the probe now sets DontChase before each retreat step (diagnostic: 14 retreats, 3 positions, 12 potions); v6 (retreat vs rules, 8 rounds) running; 2026-10-13 19:11 arena v6 (retreat probe with DontChase, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 9/9 cleared, 13.3 +- 1.9 potions, 2281 +- 337 damage, 90.5 +- 8.3 s; Spiral rules 8/8, 15.0 +- 2.7 potions, 2566 +- 387, 90.2 +- 10.1 s; no deaths; 11% fewer potions and less damage at equal time, the simulator's direction at about a third of its predicted size (8.8 vs 12.4 per clear), not yet significant (Welch t -1.44, a retreat run beats a rules run in 68% of pairs); 8 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 19:57 arena v6 final (16-17 runs each, clean live layer, heal 160): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 16/17 cleared, 88.4 +- 9.8 s, 13.1 potions on cleared runs, 2178 +- 491 damage taken; Spiral rules 16/16, 88.2 +- 11.8 s, 14.9 potions, 2544 +- 432 damage; no deaths; damage -14% (Welch t ~ -2.3), potions -13% (t -1.93; one-sided p ~0.03 for the direction the simulator predicted beforehand), equal clear time: the first live effect of a simulator-designed policy, about half the simulator's predicted size; one retreat run never cleared (it retreated out of the fight: 806 gate drops, no kills), a failure mode to handle (re-engage when no attacker is adjacent); 2026-10-13 20:39 arena v6 FINAL (23-24 runs each, clean live layer, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv since 18:21): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 23/24 cleared, 12.6 potions on cleared runs, 2125 damage taken, 88.6 s; Spiral rules 23/23, 15.5 potions, 2639 damage, 91.7 s; no deaths; potions -19% (Welch t -3.89), damage -19% (t -4.20), clear time not different (t -0.96): the first statistically clear live win, for a policy the simulator found and evolution rediscovered (the simulator predicted -29%); vBot was at 14.1-14.8 potions in v4/v5 under the same live layer, a head-to-head retreat vs vBot round is next; 2026-10-14 00:23 PAUSED at the user's request (account switch): arena v7 (retreat vs vBot, arena-results-cyclops-v7.tsv) stopped after 8 vBot and 7 retreat runs (retreat 11-15 potions, vBot 8-18; summarize with arena-summary.ps1); next on resume: finish v7, rescan the arena at radius 12 (probe-scan-body.lua, live knight leaves the +-7 window), mixed cyclops+troll camp probe (cavebot 240 potions/37.7 s vs evolved rules 431/43.5 s per 200 clears: rules tuned for cyclops lose on mixed camps); 2026-10-14 01:59 arena v7 final (retreat vs vBot, clean live layer, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v7.tsv since 2026-10-13 23:30, 20 retreat / 21 vBot runs, all cleared, no deaths): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 12.1 sd 1.8 potions, 2083 sd 263 damage taken, 89.3 sd 10.3 s; vBot 13.8 sd 3.3 potions, 2371 sd 502 damage, 92.4 sd 13.4 s; potions -13% (Welch t -2.14, df 31, one-sided p 0.02), damage -12% (t -2.32, one-sided p 0.014), clear time not different (t -0.85): retreat beats vBot on supplies and damage at equal speed, smaller than its -19% margin over rules in v6; vBot is also less consistent (potion sd 3.3 vs 1.8); live layer asymmetry found: probe-vbot-body.lua samples experience and health only every 10 s, so vBot clear times are rounded up to the next 10 s (about +5 s bias: corrected vBot clear 87.4 s, t +0.50, still no difference) and vBot lowest health is a 10 s sample, not a true minimum; the vBot probe now also watches every 100 ms for v8 on; v7 pools two policy snapshots (23:29 and 00:31) whose only difference is an additive Scored targeting case in policy.spi that live.spi does not use; 2026-10-14 02:18 arena spot rescanned at radius 12 (probe-scan-body.lua, tibia-local/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt: raw grid, 25 row bitmasks with bit i = column dx -12+i is #, and a client-loaded check): the knight was centered at 1933,1350 in that scan (one tile off the 1932,1349 reset; a second scan logged in at 1932,1349, so the knight's login tile varies run to run); the radius-12 scan cannot see past the client's loaded 18x14 window (x 1924..1941, y 1343..1356 in both scans): g_map.getTile returns nil outside it and the probe prints nil as #, so the outer band of solid # rows and columns is unknown terrain, not walls (probe-scan-unknown-body.lua prints ? there); a wider live map needs the knight to walk the area or a server-side or OTBM read, not a bigger client scan radius; inside the window the grid matches the radius-7 scan; 2026-10-14 03:24 arena v8 (heal below 120 for both, Spiral rules vs vBot, 10 runs each, arena-results-cyclops-v8.tsv since 2026-10-14 02:18, first round with the vBot probe watching experience and health every 100 ms): all 20 cleared, no deaths; Spiral rules 84.4 sd 6.0 s, 12.8 sd 1.6 potions, 2233 sd 235 damage, lowest health mean 67 (min 52); vBot 88.8 sd 16.0 s, 13.2 sd 3.7 potions, 2299 sd 572 damage, lowest mean 65 (min 28); no significant difference (Welch t -0.82 time, -0.31 potions, -0.34 damage); against heal 160 (v4-v7) both drink 1-2 fewer potions at equal damage and speed and run about 35-40 hp closer to death, still survivable with 3 cyclops; vBot stays the less consistent one (sd 3.7 potions, its two worst runs bottomed at 28 and 30 hp); earlier rounds' vBot lowest health (mean 169-192 at heal 160) was a 10 s sampling artifact, so vBot never had the larger safety margin those tables showed; 2026-10-14 03:32 vBot probe now stops at clear (100 ms watch, finish 'cleared', post-finish HealBot drinks not counted); smoke run cleared 93.7 s, 13 potions, lowest 109, log ends right after clear; 2026-10-14 04:43 arena v9 cyclops 12+12, retreat at 2, ReachFirst (spiral-retreat) vs CurrentFirst (spiral-retreat-current): potions 13.3+-2.6 vs 13.5+-3.4 (t -0.14), damage 2243+-373 vs 2290+-482 (t -0.27), clear 90.1+-9.0 vs 92.6+-11.8 s (t -0.59); all cleared, 0 deaths; no difference on the three metrics. Post-hoc: lowest health 91.6+-28.9 vs 113.1+-12.1 (t -2.38, two reach runs dipped to 34/36) - CurrentFirst never went below 93; 2026-10-14 04:59 arena v9 vBot reference (fixed probe, stops at clear, block after the Spiral runs, not interleaved) n=6: potions 14.0+-3.6, damage 2418+-575, clear 91.1+-9.9 s, 0 deaths; vs spiral-retreat t potions -0.40, damage -0.68, clear -0.21; vs spiral-retreat-current t -0.28, -0.47, +0.29 - no significant difference; vBot runs now ~2.8 min instead of ~3.8; 2026-10-14 05:51 arena v9 pooled (12 alternating + 6 interleaved with vBot, all cleared, 0 deaths): ReachFirst vs CurrentFirst n=18/18 potions 12.7+-2.3 vs 13.4+-3.2 (t -0.72), damage 2172+-326 vs 2263+-462 (t -0.68), clear 89.6+-9.1 vs 91.7+-11.3 s (t -0.61) - no difference, ReachFirst nominally ahead; lowest-health gap did not replicate (pooled 97.2 vs 109.2, t ~-1.6). vBot (fixed probe) n=12: potions 14.1+-3.2, damage 2397+-492, clear 90.7+-10.9; spiral-retreat vs vBot t potions -1.27, damage -1.39, clear -0.29 (interleaved-only n=6/6: potions t -2.06, damage t -1.80); 2026-10-14 05:53 all 12 v9 vBot logs end 'finish: cleared' (no run complete/timeout, 0 post-finish drinks); v8 vBot logs had 0 potions after clear either, so the old 150 s tail cost wall time only and did not bias v8 potions/damage. v9 95% CI ReachFirst-CurrentFirst: potions -0.7 [-2.6,+1.2], damage -91 [-363,+181], clear -2.1 s [-9.1,+4.9]; 2026-10-14 05:54 pooled verdict, retreat (ReachFirst) vs vBot over v7 and v9 (38 vs 33 runs, potions from server messages, unaffected by the old vBot sampling): 12.4 vs 13.9 potions, -11%, Welch t -2.36, same clear time; v9 alone (vBot via the fixed probe, 12 runs) t -1.27, so the effect is real but modest; damage pooled not quoted because log matching picked up extra vBot logs (44 logs vs 33 rows); targeting during retreats (ReachFirst vs CurrentFirst) is a wash live (18 each, |t| < 0.8); 2026-10-14 06:38 CORRECTION of the vBot claim: arena v10 (9 more pairs, 05:55-06:38, arena-results-cyclops-v10.tsv) went the other way (retreat 13.6 vs vBot 13.0 potions); pooled v7+v9+v10 (47 vs 42 runs): retreat 12.6 vs vBot 13.7 potions (-8.2%, Welch t -1.89, not significant), clear 90.7 vs 92.0 s, no deaths; the two rounds with identically measured probes (v9+v10) give t -0.75; verdict: the retreat policy is level with vBot, perhaps slightly better; it clearly beats our rules policy (-19%, t -3.89); the v7 result was a high draw that regressed; lesson: decide the run count before looking (sequential peeking inflated the first claim); 2026-10-14 08:37 nExBot prepared as the second open-source baseline: pinned at 19632d4 (v4.0.4, default branch head 2026-07-15; the benchmark table said pushed 2026-09-01, other branches), copied to tibia-local/bots/nExBot-19632d4 without git/tests/docs; its README links an MIT LICENSE file that is missing from the repo (matters for publication only); it ships an auto-updater and an analytics module that call GitHub and nexbot.cc, so tibia-local/bot-network-sandbox.lua stubs g_http, HTTP and g_platform.openUrl for every competitor (silent no-ops; the updater's no-HTTP fallback would open a browser); its HealBot compares every potion threshold against HP percent, even rules marked absolute HP, so parity with heal-below-160 is HP% 31 (about +-5 hp); probe-nexbot-body.lua selects config 'nExBot'; next, after PR-1 and PR-2: one live run to let it create its per-character UnifiedStorage, then seed HealBot.json, targetbot_configs/arena.json and the storage the way vBot is seeded", Feature, P1, D5, 85u32, Active, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,benchmark", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_baselines () = Planning ("TIBIA-BASELINES", Minutes 2400u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 1u32, "2026-10-14T13:58Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 09:58 nExBot seeding prepared offline (read-only reading of nExBot 19632d4): HealBot.json in bot/nExBot/nExBot_configs/profile_{0,1}/ (same profile shape as vBot); the engine collapses HP and HP% into one hp threshold compared to floor(health*100/max) with <=, so heal below 160 at 515 max is hp% <= 30 (fires for health <= 159, exact); UnifiedStorage at nExBot_configs/characters/knight sample/UnifiedStorage.json (targetbot.enabled, selectedConfig arena, healbot.enabled), and vbot-arena.json is format-compatible (targeting/looting). The network sandbox is prepended to the runtime copy of _Loader.lua. Staged in run-policy-scenario.next.ps1 (-Bot nExBot) and run-arena.ps1 (competitor nexbot); swapped in after PR-1. Earlier note said 31%: that was wrong (floor semantics).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 2u32, "2026-10-14T14:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 10:30 CORRECTION: every live spiral-* run since 2026-10-13 11:48 ran with vBot's HealBot and TargetBot active alongside our policy (the vBot probe enabled the client's bot setting for the character; nothing reset it; the policy probe never disabled it). Signature: server-reported potions our policy never drank in almost every spiral run (tibia-local/harness-check.ps1 scans all logs). All live policy comparisons and the live check of the simulator's clear prediction are therefore hybrids; PR-1 is void and stopped at 61 rows. Fix: run-policy-scenario writes the bot node per competitor and removes other bots' folders, the policy probe disables the bot before login, and run-arena records foreign potions/actions per run. Re-measurement: BENCHMARK PR-4. Server-mechanics fidelity rows and the 10-13 03:34 troll targeting run are unaffected.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 3u32, "2026-10-14T18:53Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 14:53 PR-4 (fixed harness, 30 runs each, 0 harness failures, 0 deaths): potions rules 11.53, retreat 12.90, vBot 14.00; retreat vs vBot difference -1.10 (CI -2.62 .. 0.42, t -1.45) no difference shown; retreat vs rules +1.37 (t 1.82) no difference shown, direction against retreat. Clear times 87.6 / 91.3 / 92.7 s match the simulator's 88.6 / 88.1; potions do not (predicted 13.23 rules, 9.09 retreat; t -3.69 and 6.44). The live retreat win and the 'simulator predicts live' claim from the hybrid runs are withdrawn.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 4u32, "2026-10-14T20:31Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:31 live random control (PR-5, probe-random-body.lua, 10 runs, clean): 94.1 potions per clear (simulator 90.5, holds), 102.7 s (simulator 117.0, gap: live auto-attack persists between random picks). Control far below rules 11.5, retreat 12.9, vBot 14.0.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 5u32, "2026-10-14T20:33Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 16:33 nExBot: 3/3 PR-3 check runs crash the client (TIBIA-NEXBOT-CRASH); PR-3 not run today.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 6u32, "2026-10-15T07:06Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 03:06 PR-8 (pre-registered replication, rules vs vBot, 30 each, clean): 12.90 vs 14.17 potions, difference -1.27 (CI -2.99 .. 0.46), t -1.47: no difference shown; PR-4's descriptive 11.53 for rules did not replicate. Both Spiral policies sit ~1.2 potions below vBot without significance at n=30.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 7u32, "2026-10-15T10:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 05:50: nExBot 4.0.4 is now a running baseline (three harness shims, BENCHMARK PR-3a). Pre-registered results on the clean harness: retreat vs vBot no difference shown (PR-4, t -1.45), rules vs vBot no difference shown (PR-8, t -1.47), retreat vs nExBot significant (PR-3a, 12.2 vs 14.6 potions, t -2.14, narrow). Left: OTCv8 bot module, scripted cavebot as a live competitor.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 8u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: open parts: OTCv8 bot module, scripted cavebot as a live competitor, and nExBot's license (see TIBIA-ARENA-RELEASE).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 9u32, "2026-10-15T11:04Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:04 correction: nExBot's license is not a task (no interaction with public projects); open parts are the OTCv8 bot module and a scripted cavebot as a live competitor.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 10u32, "2026-10-15T16:54Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 12:54 PR-9 (pre-registered 08:13, 50 runs each): Spiral rules 12.46 vs vBot 14.66 potions per cyclops clear, diff -2.20 (CI -3.35..-1.05), Welch t -3.80: SIGNIFICANT, rules use fewer potions; same clear time (88.7 vs 87.9 s), 0 deaths, damage 2145 vs 2479 (the saving is damage avoided). First well-powered live win over an open-source baseline. One disclosed interim look at 10:37 (fixed n, no early stop).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 11u32, "2026-10-15T18:14Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 14:14 PR-9 explained (post-hoc): the whole rules-vs-vBot difference is the knight's login protection. Canary ends it on the player's own move/autowalk/turn/say/item use/attack cancel, not on starting an attack; our probe keeps it, vBot ends it. Hits in the first 10 s: vBot 9.14, rules 1.58; after 10 s level (60.1 vs 60.4). So PR-9 measures a scenario artifact, not hunting skill. Harness fix next: end the protection for every competitor right after login (one native turn outside the parity gate), then re-test rules vs vBot (PR-11).")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 12u32, "2026-10-15T22:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:40 PR-11 (pre-registered 14:21; parity.lua now ends login protection for every competitor with one native turn after login): rules 14.42 vs vBot 14.78 potions, diff -0.36 (CI -1.58..0.86), t -0.58: NO DIFFERENCE SHOWN; hits 69.1 vs 69.2, first 10 s 9.6 vs 9.0, clear 88.3 vs 87.4 s, 0 deaths. Our rules policy and vBot are level; PR-9's win was the login-protection artifact. Next for a real win: a behavior that changes exposure live (the model's policy effects are too strong, PR-10), not thresholds.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 13u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 remaining harness asymmetry after the protection fix: parity.lua ends login protection at 0.3 s for everyone, but the policy probe starts deciding about 2.5 s after login while vBot acts at once (PR-11 first-10-s hits 9.6 vs 9.0, consistent). Does not change PR-11's no-difference verdict; a test for a win should start every competitor's logic at the same moment. Recorded in BENCHMARK.md Parity.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 14u32, "2026-10-17T20:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-17 16:28 paused (user). On resume: TIBIA-START-SYNC, then run the written PR-12 (fair nExBot re-test); the OTCv8 module and a scripted live cavebot stay open.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 15u32, "2026-10-18T19:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:30 resuming per the 10-17 note: TIBIA-START-SYNC is implemented (uncommitted, verification in today's live block), and PR-12 is amended in docs/BENCHMARK.md before any run: both competitors start at login + 2.5 s, and runs go in chunks across days into results/arena-results-cyclops-pr12.tsv, still with no interim looks. First chunk planned for today's live block after the start-sync and stray-server checks: alternating spiral-retreat and nexbot, cyclops pack v1, heal 160, level 30, axe 60, experience 675.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 16u32, "2026-10-18T19:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:42 PR-12 chunk 1 started at 15:42: run-arena -Runs 10 alternating spiral-retreat / nexbot (cyclops 3, level 30, axe 60, heal 160, retreat at 2, experience 675) into results/arena-results-cyclops-pr12.tsv, with synchronized starts (TIBIA-START-SYNC verified live 15:41). No looks at potions until all 40 per competitor are in.")
inl note_of_tibia_baselines_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-BASELINES", 17u32, "2026-10-18T20:40Z", "tibia-lane", "PR-12 chunk 1 done 2026-10-18 16:40: 20 rows (10 spiral-retreat, 10 nexbot, alternating, synchronized starts at login+2.5 s) in results/arena-results-cyclops-pr12.tsv. Outcomes not inspected (no interim looks per the PR-12 amendment); more chunks on later days.")
