inl test_expect_diagnostic () = Task ("TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC", "Split from SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES: a test block whose expectation is a compiler diagnostic, so negatives live in the .spi beside the code (today a test header takes only static/print_code/ignore and passes on exit 0; Brzozowski alone has 31 negative_* folders); proposal: `test name rejects \"<diagnostic text or code>\" =`, compiled but expected to fail with a matching diagnostic; Kino reports it like any test; user decision 2026-10-12 19:05: error code + message substring, e.g. test rejects_mixed_units fails EJP0040 \"Unification failure\" = (code exact, text substring); 19:52 Kino lane (uncommitted): header test x fails EJP0040 \"Unification failure\" = (code optional: fails \"msg\"), round-trips .spi -> cell (///- --test --fails ...) -> .spi byte for byte, report mode fails; passes only when compiling prefix+body fails with a diagnostic containing the message and, if given, the code; compiling anyway, a different diagnostic or a failure after compiling fail; a matching message without any E code fails with carries no error code; stub tests 26/26; real run: rejects_mixed and rejects_unbound passed, needs_code failed as designed because type-checker errors carry no code", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "tests,compiler,kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_test_expect_diagnostic () = Planning ("TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_report_targets () = Task ("KINO-REPORT-TARGETS", "Run report lists the targets each test ran with a verdict and timing per target: coins.spi tests with ///> c pass, but the report and the cell show one output and an empty unavailable list, so nobody can tell whether C ran; 19:49 Kino lane (uncommitted): each report row and each cell's spiral_test metadata has targets: [{target, status, ms}], one per ///> line (rust for the default host); status passed | failed | unsupported | not_run (a later target after an earlier one failed); ms = that target's compile + build + run; recalled tests show the targets stored with the memo entry; Spiral.Kino.last_targets() per run; report/notebook/memo tests 34/34; real run math.spi 79 s 15/15 (atan2: gleam 10.3 s, lua 4.3 s, fsharp 16.8 s, cuda 6.1 s; plain rust tests 8-17 s); 2026-10-13 18:35 Kino lane: two more runnable targets on this machine: ///> lean (lean --run on the harness toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc4: SPIRAL_LEAN, else the toolchain's own lean under ELAN_HOME, ~/.elan or scoop elan, else PATH) and ///> delphi via fpc -O2 -Mdelphi when dcc32 is absent (was unsupported); target_audit 14/14 targets ok (failing twin fails with its text, passing twin passes) incl. lean and delphi; sm' show_floats asserts one string on 10 targets", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_report_targets () = Planning ("KINO-REPORT-TARGETS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_queue_latency () = Task ("KINO-QUEUE-LATENCY", "Queue time dominates a test cell: coins.spi cell phases_ms queue 8216, compile 3300, target 1899 of 13581 (2026-10-12, warm daemon, other lanes active); measure queue under no load, then fix ordering/parallelism; complements KINO-RESULT-MEMO; 2026-10-13 12:19 Kino lane: queue time was compiles serialized behind one compiler plus unit-ending test bodies compiling twice; fixed by single compiles for _assert-ending tests (damage.spi per-test 11.8-15.7 s -> 5.6-8.7 s) and the memory-sized compiler pool (3 sessions: queue p50 26.5 s -> 10.5 s); remaining queue is genuine contention when memory keeps the pool at one compiler", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,perf", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_queue_latency () = Planning ("KINO-QUEUE-LATENCY", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_startup_cost () = Task ("KINO-STARTUP-COST", "Fixed cost per run: one filtered test (--test diagonal_headings on geometry.spi) took 22.9 s versus 44.9 s for all 8, so ~15-20 s is startup (mix boot, daemon handshake, prefix compile); measure the split and cut it; target: one unchanged test under 1 s with KINO-RESULT-MEMO; 18:25 Kino lane (uncommitted): fully memoized math.spi via run_notebook.ps1 7.94 s -> 4.78 s; spi/domain_compiler.ex gleam_stale?/1 skips gleam build when beams are newer (compile check 5.6 -> 4.0 s same load); memo key normalizes the compiler DLL path (wrapper backslashes vs Kino default made every direct mix/evaluate run miss: 0 -> 15 hits, test added, memo+report 19/19); remaining ~3 s is Elixir+mix boot, 0.5-1.2 s pwsh: next cut is KINO-WARM-RUNNER; 20:04: superseded by KINO-WARM-RUNNER (fully memoized file ~1.2-1.4 s end to end, most of it pwsh startup)", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,perf", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_startup_cost () = Planning ("KINO-STARTUP-COST", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_multi_path_output () = Task ("KINO-MULTI-PATH-OUTPUT", "run_notebook with several --path refuses --output-path (\"take a single --path\"), so a multi-file run writes .ipynb files next to the sources; add --output-dir (skip if the Kino lane already tracks it); 16:25 Kino lane: run_notebook.ps1 / mix spiral.notebook take --output-dir <dir> with several --path, writing each <name>.ipynb there (created if missing; --output-path still needs a single --path); spiral-tests lines per file plus a total; unit tests green, uncommitted; verified 17:20 by the tibia lane (port 13935): --output-dir with --path wire.spi --path creatures.spi exit 0, both .ipynb written, per-file spiral-tests lines + total (11 passed, memo_hits 2)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino", "current", "current")
