inl note_of_bundler_debug_stack_overflow_1 () = Note ("BUNDLER-DEBUG-STACK-OVERFLOW", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:38Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:38 touch: cause is not the code shape but Debug's missing .tail calls: init/recinl/rectype recurse through Hopac promise continuations (x.block >>** fun ...); fix candidate: <Tailcalls>true</Tailcalls> in SpiralCompilerCore.fsproj (Release already defaults to it, so Release output is unchanged); to verify with a Debug build on mega_brzozowski_derivatives")
inl note_of_bundler_debug_stack_overflow_2 () = Note ("BUNDLER-DEBUG-STACK-OVERFLOW", 2u32, "2026-10-14T13:34Z", "main-thread", "09:34 related overflow found and fixed in source (not the bundler): a Release compile overflows in the typechecker at about 1500+ sequential lets in one body, because infer ran on a Hopac worker stack (peval already has its 1.5 GB thread). infer now runs on a 256 MB thread (inferOnLargeStack). Both changes ride the next pack, where the Debug build also checks mega_brzozowski with Tailcalls.")
inl note_of_bundler_debug_stack_overflow_3 () = Note ("BUNDLER-DEBUG-STACK-OVERFLOW", 3u32, "2026-10-14T16:31Z", "main-thread", "12:31 big-body overflow fixed at the root (pack-1d candidate): the typechecker, its deferred fill and the prepass all run as Hopac jobs on worker threads with the default stack. Each per-call wrapper only moved the overflow to the next stage. Fix: Program.fs sets Hopac's Scheduler.Create MaxStackSize = 256 MB for both cores; the core wrappers are reverted. With pack-1d, 2000- and 3000-let bodies compile and run (236 and 228, both checked by hand) and the 1000-module corpus compiles in 93.8 s. Regression sample: samples/typecheck_long_let_body. The Debug mega_brzozowski check (Tailcalls) still needs a Debug build.")
