inl note_of_eoie_repo_state_4 () = Note ("EOIE-REPO-STATE", 4u32, "2026-10-18T19:53Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 15:53 landed: crate eoie_repo_state, eoie repo state <root>... runs git status --porcelain=v2 --branch and log -1 once per root; typed entry_kind union and change_counts record parse porcelain v2 (renames report the new path, paths keep spaces), per-area tally over two path levels, sorted by change count, top 12 shown with a hidden-count line; e2e on eoie, spiral and x; Spiral tests 2/2")
inl eoie_agent_guide () = Task ("EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE", "generated guide every client reads (AGENTS.md section, Claude/Codex/Grok/OpenCode/Zed): per intent, the eoie call that replaces the pwsh/python habit, with worked examples, generated from the command spec so it never drifts; plus a recurring sweep that reports each client's remaining pwsh/python share as the adoption metric; source: transcript sweep 2026-10-13 22:13 over ~45k tool calls (claude 41.6k, codex 2.0k, opencode 1.1k, grok 0.2k; zed 8 threads parsed, tool shape not yet recognized); report in main's job tmp/sweep/intent-report.txt; 2026-10-14 02:16 lane 3 draft in scratch (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\one-call\\agent-guide.md, the real guide is generated once eoie do exists): how each client makes the one call (Claude Code PowerShell here-string, Codex one exec_command instead of Promise.allSettled fan-outs, OpenCode shell, Grok run_terminal_command replacing read_file 101 + grep 58 + search_replace 29, Zed pending thread parsing), then 27 habit -> eoie rows grouped read/search, edit, tables, git, processes, each with calls per client from the 2026-10-14 cluster re-mine (largest: read+search 1,829 C1629/X173/O30, read+walk 841, read+write+replace 725, read+clock 716), mapped to spec/one-call.md cases 1-33; adoption metric: multi-intent pwsh/python share per client and cluster; typo in the note above: read+search is 1,832 calls, not 1,829", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "EOIE-ONE-CALL", "eoie,one-call,adoption", "current", "current")
inl note_of_eoie_agent_guide_1 () = Note ("EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:25Z", "lane-a", "08:25 lane-a: generator prototype lane-a\\one-call\\guide-from-spec.ps1: one-call.md -> guide section (33 intents, recorded-call counts, the exact eoie do program each) so the guide cannot drift from the spec; output agent-guide.generated.md. Real one lands with eoie do.")
inl note_of_eoie_agent_guide_2 () = Note ("EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE", 2u32, "2026-10-14T15:16Z", "main-thread", "11:16 friction (main): 'agile set <root> ID progress 90' answered 'progress must be 0..100'. A non-numeric word in the progress slot reads as an out-of-range number; better: name the slot, show the word received, print the usage line.")
inl note_of_eoie_agent_guide_3 () = Note ("EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom: new friction for the guide: agile note text with embedded double quotes is split by PowerShell's native argument passing (received 6 operands). The guide should say to avoid inner double quotes or pass the text from a file.")
inl eoie_idiomatic_core () = Task ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", "rewrite eoie's core as idiomatic Spiral the way apps/tibia is going: a GADT command algebra (operation indexed by its receipt type), existential handlers, HKT-style receipt/result views, no rust_global or !!!! macro blobs; Rust stays the compiled target (rayon for parallel walk/search); keep the 1000-line crate gate, which is paying off; foundation for the one-call verbs; source: transcript sweep 2026-10-13 22:13 over ~45k tool calls (claude 41.6k, codex 2.0k, opencode 1.1k, grok 0.2k; zed 8 threads parsed, tool shape not yet recognized); report in main's job tmp/sweep/intent-report.txt; 2026-10-14 03:56 lane 3 typed design of eoie do (not compiled; C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\eoie-do\\model.spi, 939 lines, no macros, plus cases.md): GADT statement effect receipt error with 29 constructors (Edit/Write/Copy staged_write; Show/Around/Excerpt/Search/Files/Dirs/GroupLines/Nearest/Json/Table/Diff/Hash/Env/Exists/Errors/Processes/GitHistory/GitStatus/GitLog pure_read; Run/Stop/Wait/JobStart/JobWait/GitInit/GitCommit external_effect), one receipt record and one error union per statement kind, existential handles (exists kind. handle kind * handle_target kind for process/job/output), receipt views as prototypes (receipt_tallies, receipt_lines, error_lines, error_exit), effect_policy prototype for rayon fan-out (per file/dir/repo inside a statement, across consecutive pure/staged statements between barriers, never across external effects); reuse: text-replace expectations, exact_replace and batch-write commit engine with rollback, parallel_search walk/sort, fs-read/slice/context/list, fs-copy, hash, process/observation, batch-plan step algebra, rooted paths; replaced: patch/fs-actions/fs-batch-write/batch-plan file-then-call entry points and the patch plan grammar, macro blobs move behind one Rust-boundary module per capability", Story, P1, D8, 0u32, Planned, "EOIE-ONE-CALL", "eoie,one-call,adoption", "current", "current")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_1 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:22Z", "lane-a", "08:22 lane-a: rewrite baseline (git ls-files eoie/src): 309 packages; hand-written Rust 90 files/25.4k lines + 26 Rust test files/2.1k lines (no .spi sibling), generated 71/29.7k; rust_global 390 (top: contracts_entry 48), !!!! 2,319.")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_2 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom: unchanged; lane B added one more Spiral owner tonight (eoie_dev_spiral_tests, Spiral only), and rust_global sites are 261 (source-topology 10-15).")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_3 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:55Z", "main-thread", "06:55 groom: a different cut than lane A's baseline (90 files/25.4k lines): 188 tracked .rs under eoie/src, of which 26 files / 2,061 lines sit in directories with no .spi at all, the hand-written islands with no Spiral owner. Those 26 are the first rewrite targets.")
