inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_4 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-10-14T23:28Z", "lane-b", "proof: a Spiral test block (Rust backend) drives eoie.exe agile edit+show --json on a temp root and passes via run_notebook in 9 s; a 361 control fails. Macro trap: \\\" and \\# unescape; raw strings need r\\#. Draft at lane-b tmp eoie-spiral-test")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_5 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-10-15T03:37Z", "lane-b", "23:37 lane B: planning_cli.rs converted to granular Spiral test blocks (draft tmp/lane-b/eoie-spiral-test/planning_cli.spi, not landed): typed fixture_root nominal, cli_run record, agile_call union (RootThen | ModeThenRoot), one small macro per concern (temp root, state read/write, spawn eoie with tab-split args, contains/count/offset), expect/accepted/rejected in Spiral; both former tests with every assertion are test blocks; run_notebook (Kino copy + scratch host, EOIE_BIN_UNDER_TEST=eoie.exe): 2/2 passed in 41 s; control with 361m/301m expectations: 2/2 failed with 'missing estimate=361m ... in: eoie agile edit ok ... estimate=360m'; macro trap: \\$'*!left == *!right' does not parse (ETY-MissingBody), (&*!left).eq(&*!right) does; next: land it in src/agile_planning_rollup beside planning_rollup.spi, wire a test-block phase into the eoie-dev workflow, then git rm tests/planning_cli.rs")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_6 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-10-15T04:52Z", "lane-b", "00:52 lane B: LANDED (uncommitted, eoie): src/agile_planning_rollup/planning_cli.spi (both planning_cli.rs tests as granular Spiral test blocks); runner = eoie-dev workflow (src/eoie_dev_model workflow.spi + host.spi, dev.rs regenerated with pack-1f): after cargo test succeeds, every registered notebook (typed registry union rec spiral_test_notebooks: cargo package + path) whose package is selected (or all when no --package) runs through Kino spi/run_notebook.ps1 with EOIE_BIN_UNDER_TEST = the freshly built target/debug/eoie, memo off (results depend on the binary), output target/spiral-tests/*.ipynb; Kino found via EOIE_SPIRAL_KINO, else EOIE_SPIRAL_BUNDLE/../../kino (test-regeneration sets it), else ../spiral/apps/kino; --dry-run prints 'spiral test blocks <path>'; proof: build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease -Package agile-planning-rollup: cargo tests ok, then spiral-tests 2/2 passed, memo_hits 0; CI (.github/workflows/eoie.yml): checkout i574n/The-Spiral-Language into spiral/deps (Kino cells link |core-), setup-beam OTP 27/Elixir 1.18, mix deps.get in spiral/apps/kino; user: git rm src/agile_planning_rollup/tests/planning_cli.rs once CI is green")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_7 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-10-15T07:00Z", "lane-b", "03:00 lane B: the phase runs Kino with SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process (no shared daemon left resident on 13905 beside renewals/cold budgets); proofs on pack-1g: build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease -Package agile-planning-rollup without any port env 2/2 with 0 daemons before/after; staged path test-regeneration -Package agile-planning-rollup -Test -SkipRelease 2/2 (Kino via EOIE_SPIRAL_BUNDLE); full build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease earlier: 267 cargo results ok + 2/2; CI's test-dev-workflow selects only its fixture package, so the phase never runs before the compiler build step")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_8 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 8u32, "2026-10-15T08:39Z", "lane-b", "04:39 lane B: renewal preflight caught eoie_dev at 1,016 lines (> 1000 gate) from the inlined phase; moved the phase into its own Spiral owner src/eoie_dev_spiral_tests (registry.spi typed notebook registry + selection, notebook.spi run_notebook spawn + dry-run announce, main.spi run loop + Export eoie_dev_spiral_tests_run; spiral_tests.rs 76 lines), eoie_dev_model calls it via one host macro line; dev.rs 701 (694 at HEAD); source-topology ok (crate max 995, file max 982); full build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease: 269 cargo results ok + Spiral tests 2/2")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_9 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 9u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: 2 of planning_cli.rs's tests now run as Spiral test blocks inside build.ps1 -Test (269 + 2/2, renewal 04:57 covers it). Next grain: the next hand-written tests/*.rs by size; planning_cli.rs git rm waits for the first green CI with the Kino step.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_10 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 10u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: planning_cli.rs deleted after green CI 38725303020 (Spiral blocks 2/2 there); its 2 tests pinned ///> rust for the Kino zig default; eoie-dev-spiral-tests now declares test-requires-cli (its notebooks launch the CLI, so a stale binary passed before); 2 new registered notebooks (agile_todo_model model.spi 5 tests, todo_cli.spi 3).")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_11 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 11u32, "2026-10-19T23:00Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 19:00 eoie-lane: binary-driving Rust tests become Spiral notebooks on a shared harness package src/eoie_cli_harness (module cli: fixture roots, cli_args union, eoie_run/racing/closing-stdout runs, receipt normalizers, digests, symlink-or-skip, rustc_program for fake tools); notebooks include it with '///- --package ../eoie_cli_harness' + 'open cli' (a notebook compiles standalone, so this is how test code shares helpers). Ported and retired 9 Rust files (896 lines): agile_note_receipts, proxy_receipts, agile_receipts, batch_completion (eoie_contracts), agile_cache, agile_listing (eoie_agile_contracts), archive_publication, self_upgrade, eoie_cli tests/windows. New notebooks: agile_task_notes/notes_cli 6, eoie_contracts/receipts_cli 8, eoie_agile_contracts/agile_cli 9, archive_cli 3, upgrade_cli 2, eoie_cli/windows_cli 4 = 32 tests; each passed a mutation check (mutated expectations fail exactly the mutated tests); official eoie-dev run (build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease, 5 packages, heavy job) green. Traps: a runtime (~) flag that picks between cli_args shapes makes the compile-time joined recursion diverge (EJP0011), keep shape flags static; Spiral string literals cannot hold a backslash before a quote, build it with char 92/34.")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_12 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 12u32, "2026-10-19T23:48Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 19:48 eoie-lane batch 2: native_paths.rs (4 binary tests -> eoie_coverage_prune/coverage_cli.spi with a rustc-built fake cargo; the pure eoie_coverage_jobs test -> a test block in coverage_prune_model/model.spi next to coverage_jobs_binding), evidence.rs -> eoie_coverage_prune/evidence_cli.spi (coverage-assess, prune-uncovered, coverage-export through proxy verbs, fake grcov), hygiene_confinement.rs sidecar half -> eoie_release_contracts/hygiene_cli.spi (junction helper with CREATE_NO_WINDOW). Kept in Rust on purpose: hygiene transient tests (prune-release-transients has no proxy verb; a test-only verb is not worth it), prune_transaction.rs (one case pre-creates a backup named after the test's own PID, which only collides in-process). False-pass trap found: through a binary, a refusal test passes on 'unknown proxy operation'; refusals now also assert that text is absent. Full gated release job-1792451451481 green with 34 notebooks / 99 Spiral tests, topology gate passed, eoie.exe 19:43 sha256 52FEFE97...; hand-written Rust test files 41 -> 30 (11 retired, 1 shrunk, 1,162 lines gone).")
inl note_of_eoie_spiral_tests_13 () = Note ("EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS", 13u32, "2026-10-20T00:45Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 20:45 eoie-lane batch 3: hash_boundary.rs Windows/Linux test -> eoie_proxy_search/hash_cli.spi (proxy hash with EOIE_HASH_LIMIT_BYTES=3, junction ancestor), the Rust file keeps only the Linux FIFO test (36 lines). Flake found by the official run and fixed: the agile cache fixture read the clock twice for the lease start and deadline, and eoie rejects a 1 ms skew (deadline mismatch); the fixture now reads now_ms once. Pack 12 (unaccepted) was installed at 20:36, so the rerun skips regeneration (only notebooks and the harness changed, no generated output).")
inl eoie_style_checkpoint () = Task ("EOIE-STYLE-CHECKPOINT", "Decide eoie's restart style from Tibia evidence, not before (user 2026-10-14 06:44: we still don't know if the tibia style will pay off, and it is advancing without the 1k loc restrictions); compare the two experiments on the same measures, read from git and the backlog, never from either session's opinion: lines and files per shipped feature, compile and test time per change, defects found after landing, agent edit success (edits that compiled first try), rust_global and hand-written Rust counts; eoie keeps its 1k-loc crate gate meanwhile as the control; the checkpoint runs when Tibia has shipped enough features to compare (the Tibia session owns that signal), then decides between restart in the Tibia style, restart keeping the gate, or incremental migration", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", "eoie,dogfood,spiral,decision", "current", "current")
inl note_of_eoie_style_checkpoint_1 () = Note ("EOIE-STYLE-CHECKPOINT", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:21Z", "lane-a", "08:21 lane-a: git+backlog metric script lane-a\\checkpoint\\metrics.ps1, baseline: eoie 16.8k spi + 57.2k rs lines, rust_global 390, !!!! 2,319, 0 test blocks; tibia 2.7k spi, 0 rs/macros, 163 test blocks, 304 added lines per done item. Caveats in metrics-20261014.txt.")
inl note_of_eoie_style_checkpoint_2 () = Note ("EOIE-STYLE-CHECKPOINT", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom: unchanged; source-topology 10-15: crate max 995 lines (rust_std_fs_mutation), file max 982 (compat_driver.rs), both under the 1000 gate.")
inl note_of_eoie_style_checkpoint_3 () = Note ("EOIE-STYLE-CHECKPOINT", 3u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: user 21:05: the Tibia model (free test cells, no LOC limit) is unproven at a scale magnitudes higher until it reaches a SOTA result. The one good lesson of eoie's old build is the strict 1,000-line gate on generated Rust crates while the Spiral side stays free (hopacsota will be fast); that gate should be reproduced in the next codebase big enough to need it (Tibia or a new one; the X bot is too small).")
