inl note_of_hopac_docs_reread_1 () = Note ("HOPAC-DOCS-REREAD", 1u32, "2026-10-17T13:06Z", "main-thread", "09:06 main-thread fork: API inventory done against Hopac 0.5.1's Hopac.xml (424 members; gpt5parallel uses about 20). The re-read's adoption list lives in HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH; LF-derived scheduling ideas in HOPACSOTA-LF-SCHEDULING.")
inl note_of_hopac_docs_reread_2 () = Note ("HOPAC-DOCS-REREAD", 2u32, "2026-10-19T12:11Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:11 helper-lane lap 1: cross-checked every Hopac API PLAN.md names against Hopac 0.5.1's Hopac.xml (~/.nuget/packages/hopac/0.5.1, 497 doc entries incl. types): all exist - Alt.choose/chooser/prepare/random, Job.start/queue/server/iterateServer, Hopac.run (and startWithActions for the D13 top-level handler), IVar.Now, Promise.Now(.isFulfilled), Scheduler.create/kill/run/wait, Stream.Src and Stream.Src.tap, Stream.debounce and Stream.buffer (both take a Stream, i.e. Promise of Cons, so the D14 HUD is Src.tap then debounce/buffer as written), Stream.mapPipelinedFun/Job (banned by PLAN line 351). No PLAN text names a member that 0.5.1 lacks. The full prose docs (Programming.md, Docs/*) are not on this machine; the re-read proper still needs them.")
inl note_of_hopac_docs_reread_3 () = Note ("HOPAC-DOCS-REREAD", 3u32, "2026-10-19T13:04Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:04 helper-lane lap 2: read the Hopac 0.5.1 doc comments (Hopac.xml summaries) of the members PLAN and HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH rely on; four caveats PLAN should carry: (1) Scheduler.kill: only for a local scheduler known to be idle, so the per-build scheduler (HOPAC-DEPTH adoption 1) must Scheduler.wait for idle before kill, including on the failure path where jobs may still run; (2) Job.conCollect: not optimal for fine-grained parallel execution and raises AggregateException when several jobs fail, so D16.4's codegen-per-method should chunk methods and unwrap the first diagnostic in single-flight order; (3) Stream.Src.tap returns only the remainder after the tap, so a HUD attached mid-build misses earlier fills - D14 needs a snapshot of counts plus the tapped stream; (4) IVar.fill errors on a second write while tryFill silently ignores it: D3 fill-once should use fill (double commit becomes an error, the Alt.paranoid idea) and never tryFill. Promise.Now.isFulfilled is documented as not for polling, consistent with PLAN's ban list (line 346).")
inl note_of_hopac_docs_reread_4 () = Note ("HOPAC-DOCS-REREAD", 4u32, "2026-10-19T13:41Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:41 helper-lane lap 2: DONE (lap-2 pick): re-read Hopac's prose docs (Docs/Programming.md, Docs/Internals.md) on top of the 0.5.1 reference comments, and recorded the outcome in PLAN.md itself (uncommitted): a new section Hopac 0.5.1 caveats (docs re-read 2026-10-19) before Gates every phase runs, with five bullets - Scheduler.kill only on an idle local scheduler (D5's per-compile scheduler waits first, failure path included), conCollect is coarse and raises AggregateException (D16 codegen chunks, first failure in D6 order), Stream.Src.tap sees only later events (D14 starts from a snapshot), D3 uses IVar.fill not tryFill, and choose's left bias plus withNack's lazy instantiation (as the G2 ban list and D16.2 assume) with the Gleam caveat that selectors follow mailbox order (fixes D15's table row claiming selector order; HOPACSOTA-P7). Everything else in PLAN matched the docs: deterministic left-biased choice, <*> must be safe both sequentially and in parallel with a measured sequential cutoff (Phase 3), server GC (already on: SpiralCompiler.fsproj ServerGarbageCollection true), and blocked jobs costing no thread.")
