inl note_of_eoie_status_error_values_2 () = Note ("EOIE-STATUS-ERROR-VALUES", 2u32, "2026-10-16T12:04Z", "main-thread", "08:04 main: done. eoie_agile_mutation/agile_mutation.spi agile_status_error names the valid set; regenerated with dev.ps1 -Package eoie-agile-mutation -Offline -Publish (1 owner, generated Rust diff is the one message line); build.ps1 -Test -Offline: 276 cargo results, 197 passed, 0 failed, Spiral test blocks 10/10, topology ok, eoie.exe redeployed 08:03. Live: agile set ... InProgress -> eoie error: invalid agile status (expected Planned, Active, Blocked, Paused or Done).")
inl python_backend_gaps () = Task ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", "Python backend: dynamic array runtime, UTF-8 byte strings, deep recursion, C ABI externals", TaskKind, P3, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,python,backend", "current", "current")
inl note_of_python_backend_gaps_1 () = Note ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", 1u32, "2026-10-16T10:45Z", "main-thread", "06:45 main: the 29 Python DISAGREE left after the PYTHON-INT-SEMANTICS prototype (probe single-flight-20261016-063945), stderr read on one per family: dynamic_array x11: NameError DynamicArrayReserve0 not defined (the C dynamic array runtime has no Python emission); managed_string/string_utf8 x4: IndexError string index out of range (Python indexes code points, C UTF-8 bytes: needs byte semantics like Kotlin spiralStringIndex); native_*_tail_recursion x4: RecursionError (needs sys.setrecursionlimit plus a big-stack threading main, like the other backends' 1 GB thread); abi_external x9: C ABI externals (likely out of scope for Python: mark Known or reject at compile time); array_create_reads_zero exit 705.")
inl note_of_python_backend_gaps_2 () = Note ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", 2u32, "2026-10-16T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 main: array_create_reads_zero fixed in the staged pack-1t (tmp/pack-t/python-zero-arrays.ps1: primitive arrays cp.zeros instead of cp.empty, which handed back reused memory); re-probe single-flight-20261016-064814 agrees, 28 left.")
inl note_of_python_backend_gaps_3 () = Note ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", 3u32, "2026-10-16T11:26Z", "main-thread", "07:26 main: UTF-8 family deferred by design check: lib/spiral sm'.spi Python arms are code-point based (find at 527, len at 991, slice through sm.slice at 276, split, startswith), so byte semantics in StringLength/StringIndex/StringSlice alone would mis-slice non-ASCII text in lib code. A fix must switch the primitives (helpers with an isascii fast path, surrogateescape round trip) and those arms together, then rerun the lib sweep on Python. Recursion family: staged tmp/pack-u/python-recursion.ps1 (sys.setrecursionlimit(1 << 30) at the entry; CPython 3.12 frames do not use the C stack): native_recursive_tail_recursion and native_managed_scc_tail_recursion exit 0 like C by hand; the 2 array SCC ones then hit the dynamic array gap. A 1 GB thread was rejected: Windows CPython caps threading.stack_size below 256 MB, and SystemExit inside a thread would lose exit codes.")
inl note_of_python_backend_gaps_4 () = Note ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", 4u32, "2026-10-16T11:26Z", "main-thread", "07:26 main: dynamic_array x11 and abi_external x9 are C-only samples by construction (their macros call the C runtime by name: DynamicArrayReserve0, ABI externals); in the pack-1r bless only their C rows run. They show as Python DISAGREE only because -Probe compiles every sample. Not a Python gap. Real remaining work: UTF-8 byte strings (4, needs lib arms) and the 2 SCC recursion rows (staged pack-u).")
inl note_of_python_backend_gaps_5 () = Note ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", 5u32, "2026-10-16T11:29Z", "main-thread", "07:29 main: the UTF-8 string family is PYTHON-STRINGS-UPSTREAM (existing item); this item keeps the recursion rows and the inventory.")
inl note_of_python_backend_gaps_6 () = Note ("PYTHON-BACKEND-GAPS", 6u32, "2026-10-16T13:46Z", "main-thread", "09:46 main: pack-1u installed both modes (09:16/09:21) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-092123, 6,742 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells against the pack-1s bless 073131 overridden by probes 081908 (Kotlin), 082312 (Swift), 082906 (Bend), 084211 (Python). Harness Kotlin 444, Swift 443, Bend 401, Python 422.")
inl blog () = Task ("BLOG", "Spiral blog app (user request 2026-10-16): a static blog generator written in Spiral, an app like the X client (own repo beside spiral modeled on i574n/x: per-crate .spi modules, build.ps1 with Assert-SpiralBeside, e2e.ps1, Spiral test blocks, CI) published to GitHub Pages; posts are typed Spiral data (a block union: heading, paragraph, code, terminal or benchmark output, table, note, diagram, section rule) rendered to static HTML and an RSS feed; the look and voice copy bun.com/blog: index with a featured latest card, Everything/Articles/Releases tabs, posts grouped by year with date, type label, title, blurb and authors; post pages with a large title and underline bar, byline and date, an On this page table of contents, * * * section rules, hyperfine-style terminal blocks, comparison tables, warning notes, Conclusion and a call to action; Spiral's own name, logo and colors, no Bun text or assets. First post: the overarching pipeline, written like Behind The Scenes of Bun Install: .spi source -> the compiler (one 186k-line file, single-flight and gpt5parallel cores plus the hopacsota layer, 18 backends) -> the matrix with C as oracle (6,906 rows, accept rules) -> packs (review, install both modes, accept) -> Kino -> eoie (agile backlog, one-call CLI) -> Zed and the formatter -> CI -> apps (tibia, x, dice); every number from a real run (repo C:\\home\\git\\blog = i574n/blog; generic engine/ + site/ + posts/ so forks swap content; static HTML, no Leptos)", Feature, P2, D5, 25u32, Active, "", "spiral,app,blog,dogfood", "current", "current")
inl note_of_blog_1 () = Note ("BLOG", 1u32, "2026-10-17T01:44Z", "main-thread", "21:44 main-thread research. Style source bun.com/blog (179 posts, newest Bun v1.4.3 2026-10-10). Two post kinds: Releases (H1 version, byline, tabbed install + upgrade blocks first, no prose intro, one short lead sentence + code block per feature, benchmark tables with hardware noted) and Articles (the model for the pipeline post): Behind The Scenes of Bun Install (2025-09-10, ~6-7k words) opens with a benchmark claim then a history narrative; title-case section per stage (The Problem with System Calls, Async DNS Resolution, Binary Manifest Caching, Cache-Friendly Data Layout, Multi-Core Parallelism, Conclusion); short punchy sentences, bold key ideas, code with ❌/✅ comments, hyperfine Benchmark/Summary blocks, one comparison table, captioned diagrams, a platform warning note, respectful comparisons with other tools; ends on a one-line takeaway + link. Rewriting Bun in Rust (2026-07-08): first-person, admits false starts, Stats tables, Zig:/Rust: side-by-side code. Local prior art: x/apps/client (newest app layout, copy it); dice/ui (Leptos in Spiral, older era with rust_derive.ps1 post-processing, do not copy); publish like i574n.github gh-pages.yml (workflow.ps1 -> dist -> peaceiris). Pipeline numbers at 2026-10-16: spiral_compiler.fs 186,431 lines; backends F#, C, Rust, Delphi, Zig, TypeScript, Lua, Gleam, Lean, Bend, Kotlin, Swift, Python, Wasm, WGSL, Calyx, OpenQASM, eBPF; 855 sample dirs; harness 6,906 rows, last bless single-flight-20261016-145428; lib/spiral 195 .spi/.spir; eoie 492 .spi; backlog 296 items; today 8 packs (1s-1z). Open decisions for the start: repo name (user creates it on GitHub), Pages URL, renderer backend (Rust like x).")
inl note_of_blog_2 () = Note ("BLOG", 2u32, "2026-10-17T01:56Z", "main-thread", "21:56 main-thread, UI-stack decision (user question 2026-10-16): no Leptos for the blog, neither upstream nor a port. A blog is static: HTML is produced at build time, and the only interactive part (the Everything/Articles/Releases tabs) works as one page per tab or CSS-only, so there is nothing for a reactive framework to do. Of tachys' 20.7k code lines the static-HTML part is ssr 657 + html 7.5k, mostly element and attribute tables; a typed Spiral HTML model with escaping is a few hundred lines. Measured on the local clone (v0.8.11, 2025-10): the core a port would need is ~45k code lines (tachys 20.7k, reactive_graph 12.2k, router 7.9k, meta 1.2k), and upstream is not frozen (v0.8.22 on 10-05, v0.9.0-rc0 on 10-15 changes the signal traits). Interactive Spiral UIs are a separate item, SPIRAL-UI.")
inl note_of_blog_3 () = Note ("BLOG", 3u32, "2026-10-17T01:56Z", "main-thread", "21:56 main-thread, layout decision (user 2026-10-16: repo cloned at C:\\home\\git\\blog = i574n/blog, empty): the blog machinery is a generic app and the content sits apart, so a fork only swaps two folders. engine/ = generic Spiral (post model as a block union, HTML renderer, index with tabs and year groups, RSS, table of contents from headings, routes from slugs); site/site.spi = name, logo, colors, authors, base URL; posts/<slug>/ = post.spi (typed post data: title, date, kind Article|Release, authors, blurb, blocks) plus assets; scripts/ = build.ps1, workflow.ps1, e2e.ps1 as in x. Routes: / is the index, /<slug>/ is a post, /rss.xml; the first post is posts/<pipeline-slug>/ and is the only post at first. The generator runs natively (Rust like x) and writes dist/, which gh-pages publishes. Posts are Spiral data, so a broken link to a heading, a missing date or an unknown author fails the build.")
inl note_of_blog_4 () = Note ("BLOG", 4u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: C:\\home\\git\\blog\\engine (untracked) has html, post, page, index, site and build modules with 15 tests: site = shared layout + index.html + <slug>/index.html (a fork swaps the entries); build writes the tree to a temp dir and reads it back on Rust. Next: style.css, one package at the blog root with engine/ and posts/ as module folders (the x/apps/client layout: one packageDir, folder modules), then the first post. Its blocks are not postable yet (10 over 280 X weight).")
inl note_of_blog_5 () = Note ("BLOG", 5u32, "2026-10-18T12:36Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 08:36 main-thread engine grown (C:\\home\\git\\blog\\engine, untracked, tests written but not run yet, Cells verification queued after today's bless): post.block gains Terminal (command + output, prompt span), Table (head + rows, escaped cells) and Note (aside); page renders headings with section ids and an On this page table of contents (none without headings); rss.spi is an RSS 2.0 feed with dc:date (ISO dates, no RFC 822 day-of-week math); style.spi holds the stylesheet (Spiral palette, featured card, year groups, underline title bar, * * * rules, terminal blocks, tables, notes); site emits index.html, style.css, rss.xml, articles/index.html and releases/index.html (index.only filters by kind) plus one folder per post; pipeline.spi is the first post as typed data (one compiler file and two cores, 19 targets, C and Zig oracles, packs and blesses), every block under 280 characters. Next: run the 8 modules' tests through Cells, then the one-package layout (engine/ and posts/ folders) and build.ps1/e2e.ps1/CI like x.")
inl note_of_blog_6 () = Note ("BLOG", 6u32, "2026-10-18T12:57Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 08:57 main-thread: repo scaffold in x's shape (untracked, not run): scripts/common.ps1 (BlogRoot, SpiralRoot beside, Assert-SpiralBeside, Invoke-SpiralTests through spiral's apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 with the process compiler), scripts/init.ps1 (clones spiral beside, init-app-build), scripts/build.ps1 (the 9 engine modules' test blocks), scripts/workflow.ps1, and .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml (ubuntu + windows, rust, beam 27/1.18/gleam 1.19.1, zig 0.17.0, one step: pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1). Needs actions.lock generated like the other repos (gh actions-lock), then a generator main that writes the site into dist/ and a Pages publish job; first local run of build.ps1 after today's bless.")
inl note_of_blog_7 () = Note ("BLOG", 7u32, "2026-10-18T13:47Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 09:47 main-thread repair: my 08:3x scripted edits of engine/post.spi and site.spi passed -replace expressions straight into .Replace(...) calls, where PowerShell binds the comma-separated arguments into the -replace operator, so parts of both files became empty lines (post.spi lost its union and helper functions, site.spi two match cases). The user's 09:39 blog commit c8c3da8 carries that damage. Fixed in the tree: post.spi rewritten from e92c5af's intact content plus the Terminal/Table/Note blocks, site.spi's two cases restored. Verified: a probe package that builds site.files [pipeline.entry ()] compiles to Zig on the installed compiler (all engine modules typecheck); the test blocks still need their Cells run. Needs a commit.")
inl note_of_blog_8 () = Note ("BLOG", 8u32, "2026-10-18T15:57Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 11:57 main-thread: blog CI has never been green, and the cause is one line. engine/html.spi lacked the '///- --package .' first line that the other 8 modules (and x's modules) have. Under CI's runner (run_notebook.ps1, SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER=process) its test program therefore never loads package.spiproj's packages (|core-, spiral-), and both runs (13:43Z on c8c3da8 and 15:32Z on 7a41491) stopped at html.spi:2:10 ETY-UnboundModule on 'open testing', then 'unbound sm''. It's first in build.ps1's list, so no other module ran. The local mix spiral.notebook gate resolved lib anyway, which hid it. Fixed in the tree (directive added). Verifying with scripts/build.ps1, CI's exact path, through the heavy gate. Also new: scripts/publish.ps1 plus a CI publish step and push job (TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO), and a .gitignore (/dist/, /target/).")
inl note_of_blog_9 () = Note ("BLOG", 9u32, "2026-10-18T16:34Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 12:34 main-thread: verified locally through CI's exact path, scripts/build.ps1 (run_notebook.ps1 per module, SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER=process, on the tree lib incl. git-0e's conversion and the installed 10:28 compiler). All 9 modules pass, 25/25 tests, BLOG-OK. The html.spi '///- --package .' line is the fix; it needs the user's push, then CI should be green for the first time and the push job creates gh-pages.")
inl note_of_blog_10 () = Note ("BLOG", 10u32, "2026-10-19T12:13Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:13 helper-lane lap 1: verified state: blog CI is green (tests run on 5539b84, 2026-10-18 22:13Z, success) and Pages deploys, but https://i574n.github.io/blog/ serves only the dir-tree page of the source (scripts/publish.ps1 calls spiral publish-tree.ps1; gh-pages root holds .nojekyll, README.md, _github, engine, scripts, index.html = tree). The blog site itself is never generated: engine/package.spiproj lists html, post, page, index, rss, style, site, showcase, build (pipeline.spi is not a module), and build.spi has write_files only inside a test. Missing for a real site: a generator entry that calls site.files over the posts and writes dist/, publish of dist/ beside the tree page, and the engine/ vs posts/ vs site/ split (posts and site.spi still live in engine/). Uncommitted: gh-pages.yml rust channel stable -> nightly-2026-10-18 (someone's RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE edit).")
inl note_of_blog_11 () = Note ("BLOG", 11u32, "2026-10-19T13:06Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:06 helper-lane lap 2: the missing generator, written (uncommitted, unrun): engine/generate.spi (main: showcase.entries |> site.files |> build.write_files dist, exit 0) registered last in engine/package.spiproj; generator/Cargo.toml (bin blog-generate over ../engine/generate.rs, the x crate convention with [package.metadata.spiral] entry/output; chrono as the only dep, since lib file_system tests pull it); scripts/generate.ps1 (BuildSpiral -> cargo build --release -> run in the blog root, prints BLOG-GENERATED); scripts/publish.ps1 now renames publish-tree's dist/index.html to dist/tree.html (same folder, so its relative links still work) and then generates the site into dist/, so https://i574n.github.io/blog/ becomes the blog itself (site.base_url already assumes that root) with the source tree at /blog/tree.html; .gitignore gains /generator/target/. HEAVY QUEUE: pwsh C:\\home\\git\\blog\\scripts\\generate.ps1 (~10 min).")
inl note_of_blog_12 () = Note ("BLOG", 12u32, "2026-10-19T14:23Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 10:23 helper-lane lap 3: settled the engine/posts/site split by reading spiproj usage: a spiproj has one packageDir and resolves packages by name under it, so separate posts/ and site/ PACKAGES could not reference engine/ while packageDir points at spiral/lib. But module lists take folders (lib/spiral/package.spiproj lists rust/ with rust and rust_operators inside) and a module keeps its bare name, so the split is one package at the blog root: modules engine/ (html post page index rss style site build), posts/ (showcase), site/ (generate). Sources need no reference edits; what changes is the spiproj location (packageDir ../spiral/lib), each file's ///- --package line (.. instead of .), Cargo.toml entry/output and bin path (../site/generate.*), generate.ps1's engine path and build.ps1's module list. base_url (engine site.spi line 25) belongs in site/ with generate. Also verified for the queued run: generate.ps1 matches lib.ps1 BuildSpiral(SpiPath, OutPath, Name), and the full blog build passed 10:00-10:04 (BLOG-SHOWCASE-POST note 4). Not applied: blog/engine is in the 11:40 core-switch freeze and the generator is still unrun.")
inl note_of_blog_13 () = Note ("BLOG", 13u32, "2026-10-19T16:26Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 12:26 helper-lane: the engine/posts/app split is scripted as lab/BLOG/split.ps1 (dry run by default, prints the plan and the new root package.spiproj): one package at the blog root (packageDir ../spiral/lib, |core- and spiral-) with module folders engine/ (html post page index rss style site build), posts/ (showcase) and app/ (generate; named app because a folder site/ beside the module site would read ambiguously), each file's ///- --package . becomes .., and Cargo.toml, scripts/generate.ps1, scripts/build.ps1 and common.ps1's notebook output names follow. Not applied: it moves tracked files (git shows them as moves for the user's commit) and the queued generate.ps1 run still targets engine/generate.spi; apply with -Apply after that run, then rerun build.ps1 and generate.ps1.")
inl note_of_blog_14 () = Note ("BLOG", 14u32, "2026-10-19T22:03Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:03 helper-lane lap 6: ran the queued generate row under the gate (lab/BLOG/generate-run.ps1, log lab/BLOG/generate-20261019-1757.log, 210 s including 172 s waiting for the slot): blog/scripts/generate.ps1 printed BLOG-GENERATED dist/ (7 site files) on the installed pack 10 compiler, so the generator still builds and runs after the core switch. That was the gate before applying lab/BLOG/split.ps1 (engine/ posts/ app/ folders). The split moves tracked files, which shows up as renames in the user's commit, so it waits for the user's go and is not applied here.")
inl spiral_ui () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI", "Spiral-native reactive UI library (user question 2026-10-16, later, not on the blog's path): fine-grained signals and statically typed view trees in the style of Leptos' tachys and reactive_graph, designed for Spiral rather than ported line by line. Most of tachys (52 public traits, tuple and either_of impls, 32 macro_rules) exists to make Rust monomorphize a static view tree, which Spiral's partial evaluation does directly, so the expected size is a fraction of the ~45k-line Rust core. Browser target through the TypeScript backend (no wasm toolchain), Rust and wasm optional. Gate: dice/ui and one new app rebuilt on it, and js-framework-benchmark rows next to Leptos 0.9 on the same machine. Upstream Leptos is not frozen (0.9.0-rc0 2026-10-15), so it is a reference, not a dependency", Feature, P3, D7, 0u32, Planned, "", "spiral,ui,lib", "current", "current")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI", 1u32, "2026-10-19T12:47Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:47 helper-lane lap 1: sized the gate's first consumer: dice/ui is 14 .spi files / 2,068 non-blank lines (transaction 414, dice_view 396, rpc 261, settings_view 223, use_transactions 210 ...) and calls 52 distinct leptos.* bindings 502 times. The surface is small and mostly two layers: view construction (element_to_view 98, text_fragment 74, div 22, element_to_fragment 22, td/th 19 each, tr 4, view_list_to_view 7, vec_to_view 5, on_click 3) and signals (signal_get 49, signal_get_untracked 37, new_arc_memo 17, signal_update 8, signal_set 7, create_signal 7, new_arc_rw_signal 6, use_context 8, arc_memo 4), plus log 23. So a Spiral-native UI that rebuilds dice/ui needs about 15 view primitives and 9 signal/memo/context primitives, not tachys' 52 traits; that is the concrete MVP list for the design.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI", 2u32, "2026-10-19T13:32Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:32 helper-lane lap 2: first executable sketch of the MVP surface (lab/SPIRAL-UI/ui.spi, about 45 lines): signal t = {get; set} over a mut cell, memo t = {get} (pull-based for now), union attribute (Class, Href, OnClick), union rec view (Text, Element of tag * attributes * children, Reactive of () -> view, Fragment), constructors text/element/reactive, and a let rec walk (count_elements / and let count_list). Probe main builds div[class app] { button[on_click: clicks + 1] { + }, reactive span }, sets the signal to 3 and returns count_elements * 10 + memo: C exit 36 (3 elements, memo 6), via try.ps1 + Invoke-Heavy. Covers the shapes behind dice/ui's top bindings (element_to_view, text_fragment, signal_get/set, new_arc_memo, on_click) at type level; missing for a real UI: dependency tracking (memo recomputation on signal change), effects, and an HTML/DOM renderer.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI", 3u32, "2026-10-19T15:15Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:15 helper-lane lap 3: wrote the next slice into lab/SPIRAL-UI/ui.spi (not yet run: the core-switch freeze stops bounded jobs until main's all-clear): signals are now push-based - each signal keeps a subscriber list (mut list of () -> ()), set notifies them (let rec notify), and create_memo source compute caches its value behind a dirty flag that the source's subscription sets, so get recomputes only after a change; plus an HTML string renderer (render_html / render_children / render_attributes: class and href become attributes, OnClick renders nothing, Reactive renders its current view). probe_main.spi counts recomputations through a mut counter: expected exit 1236 = HTML byte-equal to <div class=app><button>+</button><span>n</span></div> (1000) + 2 computes (200) + 3 elements (30) + doubled 6, with 5000 added if the memo recomputed without a change. Explicit source per memo for now; automatic dependency tracking (a current-observer stack) is the next step.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI", 4u32, "2026-10-19T16:00Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 12:00 helper-lane lap 5: next step written beside the explicit-source version: lab/SPIRAL-UI/ui_tracking.spi does automatic dependency tracking with a tracker record {observer : mut option of a mark-dirty callback}: a memo computes inside a scope that sets the observer to its own mark-dirty function (restoring the outer observer afterwards, so nested memos work), and every signal get subscribes the current observer, so a memo depends exactly on the signals it read. probe_tracking.spi: a memo over clicks, an unrelated signal changed in between; expected exit 2 (one computation at creation, none after the unrelated change, one after clicks changes, cached afterwards). Unrun until main's freeze all-clear; subscriptions are not yet deduplicated or dropped when a memo stops reading a signal.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI", 5u32, "2026-10-19T17:42Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 13:42 helper-lane: probe run (try.ps1 C on the installed compiler, switched core): the push-based memo + HTML renderer probe exits 1236 as predicted (HTML byte-equal, 2 computations, 3 elements, doubled 6). The tracking variant failed to compile (ETY-ExpectedMutableLayout: a mut field inside an immutable record cannot be assigned); fixed by making the tracker itself a mut cell of the observer option, rerun pending.")
